INSERT INTO `patientstories` (`id`, `title`, `slug`, `patient_image`, `story_date`, `donation_state`, `content`, `short_description`, `meta_title`, `meta_description`, `schema_code`, `created_at`)
VALUES
	(1,'Rathna Kumari','rathna-kumari','ratna-kumari_66a8a6e462d15.jpg','Wednesday, 1 April, 2020','Inactive','<h2>About Rathna Kumari</h2>\r\n<p>Rathna Kumari is 51 years old and is a mother of 2 daughters and a son. She is from Chennai. Her husband, Mastanaiah, works as a laborer in an iron factory with earnings of 12,000/- month. She has led a very difficult life for a mother, as both of her daughters became polio victims at the age of 6. They both are bedridden and require their parents&rsquo; support for their basic daily activities. Her son was not interested in studies and left school after the 10th grade. He works in garments sector where he gets paid according to his work. They live in a house sponsored by the Government.</p>\r\n<p>Rathna Kumari spends most of her time by taking care of her 2 daughters and reading the holy book. She says her happiest moments are on her children&rsquo;s birthday. She doesn&rsquo;t go outside since her daughters depend on her for support and for continuous medication else they will be affected with seizures. They are taking treatment at NIMHANS hospital.</p>\r\n<h2>Medical Details</h2>\r\n<p>In January 2015 she started feeling pain in her right breast and found a small lump. She visited a local clinic where the doctor recommended her to visit any hospital. Her neighbor suggested her to visit SK Hospital, where she was told to get a biopsy and tests from Karma lab. The results showed the presence of cancer cells. The SK hospital doctors explained the line of treatment and estimated cost for each treatment and/or test. Since they didn&rsquo;t have enough money for the treatment, her husband asked the opinion of the factory owner where he worked at.</p>\r\n<p>He advised them to take treatment in HCG Hospital, so Mastanaiah came with all the reports to HCG Hospital and met Dr. Shekar Patil who went through all the old reports and insisted her to undergo certain more test to confirm the line of treatment. The initially treatment started with the surgery to remove the lump, followed by 12 cycles of chemotherapy in day care and finally complete treatment with radiation. After the course of treatment, the doctor prescribed a tablet to take for 7 years along with annual check ups.</p>\r\n<p>Rathna Kumari continued with the treatment course by following up for 3 years and after that she stopped because she couldn&rsquo;t leave her daughters due to their health condition. After a few years there arouse a doubt whether there is a reoccurrence due to the lump coming back on her right breast.</p>\r\n<h2>Recent Updates</h2>\r\n<p>Rathnakumari has successfully completed her treatment and is on regular medication. She is glad to be back home with her family.</p>','<p>Rathna Kumari is 51 years old and is a mother of 2 daughters and a son. She is from Chennai. Rathna spends most of her time by taking care of her 2 daughters and reading the holy book.</p>','Rathna Kumari','Rathna Kumari','','2024-07-30 14:10:04'),
	(2,'Ayan Syed','ayan-syed','ayan-syed-image_66a9f614b505c.jpg','Wednesday, 1 April, 2020','Inactive','<h2>About Ayan Syed</h2>\r\n<p>Ayan Syed is a 6-year-old energetic child who loves spending time with his family. His parents work in HCG Hospital (Bangalore), his father is a Parking Guard and his mother is a Security Guard. According to his parents he is very happy when, &lsquo;Chicken&rsquo; &ndash; is prepared at home; as it is his favourite food.</p>\r\n<p>Ayan is a very smart child who loves studying and taking part in sports. He has also won &ndash; 1st Prize (LKG), at his School&rsquo;s Sports Event. Besides studying and sports; Ayan enjoys going out and likes posing for pictures. Apart from this, he is very close to his maternal grandmother and she cherishes the time spent with him.</p>\r\n<h2>Medical Details</h2>\r\n<p>When Ayan was studying in LKG, he used to get periodic-high-fever and though he was on antibiotics the fever wouldn&rsquo;t subside. Ayan was under the care of his grandmother for 2-months; as his mother was hospitalised due to complications in her second pregnancy. In a span of 2-months the child lost weight and his skin had turned yellow. After been taken to various clinics and government hospitals in Kolkata, despite the blood-tests; there were no improvements and they couldn&rsquo;t identify the cause of his sickness.</p>\r\n<p>A CT scan and some tests in another government hospital revealed the presence of a tumour in his stomach next to the liver. A surgery was conducted after 6 months of diagnosis, but unfortunately it was unsuccessful. The disease had spread to the entire liver and the biopsy confirmed it was cancer. A month after his surgery tests showed the presence of a tumour in the surgery area. The doctors conducted an additional surgery but the tumour surfaced again after a weeks&rsquo; time.</p>\r\n<p>Ayan was taken for treatment to Ambedkar Hospital in Bangalore and later to KIDWAI, where he was diagnosed with Embryonal&ndash;Rhabdomyosarcoma (ERMS).The doctors explained the line of treatment; a total time frame of 14 months and the estimation of the treatment {Chemotherapy + Radiation + Surgery}.He was taken to HCG hospital for a second opinion from Dr. Raghavendra. Ayan underwent surgery 3 more times but there seemed to be no progress as the cancer had spread to the entire liver. The only solution was to remove the infected portion of the liver. A decision was taken to wait until Ayan was 11 years and continue the treatment with radiation followed by medication and follow up every 6-months.</p>\r\n<h2>Recent Update</h2>\r\n<p>Ayan Syed has completed his treatment and is back home with his family. He loves spending time especially with his grandmother. He is yet to undergo a surgery to remove the residual tumor, this will be done once he is older.</p>','<p>Ayan Syed is a 6-year-old energetic child who loves spending time with his family. Ayan is a very smart child who loves studying and taking part in sports.</p>','Ayan Syed','Ayan Syed is a 6-year-old energetic child who loves spending time with his family. Ayan is a very smart child who loves studying and taking part in sports.','','2024-07-31 14:00:12'),
	(3,'Sharanya','sharanya','sharanya-image_66a9f6e3a909b.jpg','Wednesday, 1 April, 2020',NULL,'<h2>About Sharanya</h2>\r\n<p>Sharanya is a 12-year-old girl studying her 6th standard at Aiyyappa Government School in Bangalore. She was born and raised in Tamil Nadu, but moved to Bangalore since her father, Mr. Tony, works as an office assistant in a company in Bangalore. Her older brother goes to the same school as her and is in 8th standard. She has an elder brother who goes to the same school at 8th standard. She successfully completed her 6th standard and was unfortunately unable to continue into her 7th grade due to her illness. She is disappointed that she couldn&rsquo;t continue on with her friends and deeply misses them along with her teachers. She is very good at sports, especially running, and participated in many athletic activities at School. Her favorite hobby is drawing which she indulges in most of the time. She really enjoys drawling and expresses that it makes her so happy that she forgets her pain. Her dream is to become a doctor were she can help people who are suffering from various diseases.</p>\r\n<p>Sharanya&rsquo;s father is the only breadwinner for the family and earns 15000 rupees per month. Sharanya&rsquo;s mother is a homemaker. They live in a rented house in Bangalore. He struggles to make ends meet and usually runs out of money by the end of the month. Since his monthly income is used for maintaining the household, rent, and children education, he has no savings. The parents want the best education for their children, so they can have better jobs and lead a better life. Sharanya&rsquo;s mother is always in tears, as she cannot see her little girl in pain.</p>\r\n<h2>Medical Details</h2>\r\n<p>Sharanya was diagnosed with Acute Lymphoblastic leukemia (ALL) ten months ago, which was during her first week of 7th standard. Initially she started vomiting whatever she ate and her parents took her to a local clinic near their house. After initial examination the doctor prescribed tablets for indigestion with side effects of loose stools. She continued to be ill and parents took her to another clinic. There she underwent an USG (ultrasound) and her report detected cancer lumps in her stomach.</p>\r\n<p>Later she was taken to &ldquo;SEVEN DAYS&rdquo; hospital and the examining doctor suggested she should go to Kidwai Hospital for cancer treatment. One of her father&rsquo;s contacts told she should consult with Dr. Intezar from HCG Hospital, Bangalore. Finally in HCG Hospital she has undergone certain cycles of chemotherapy. In January 2020 she completed her chemotherapy and will be visiting the hospital for follow up care during this year.</p>\r\n<h2>Recent Update</h2>\r\n<p>Sharanya has successfully completed her treatment and is back home. She has started her online classes for 7th Grade.</p>','Sharanya is a 12-year-old girl studying her 6th standard at Aiyyappa Government School in Bangalore. She was born and raised in Tamil Nadu.','','','','2024-07-31 14:03:39'),
	(4,'Sarojamma','sarojamma','sarojamma-image_66a9f77d04638.jpg','Thursday, 2 April, 2020','NA','<h2>About Sarojamma</h2>\r\n<p>Sarojamma, a 75-year-old hardworking woman, sells flowers near Sai Baba Temple in Indiranagar. She has devoted her life to god and to her family. She is blessed with three sons, a daughter, eight grandchildren and two great grandchildren. Sarojamma&rsquo;s husband was also a flower seller but due to a urological medical condition he is bedridden. She and her husband stay with their youngest son who helps her get flowers to sell. Sarojamma&rsquo;s other two sons are working as drivers and their daughter is married.</p>\r\n<p>Sarojamma is very independent &ndash; that on her own she was able to get her grandchildren married; with her own hard earned money and presently is very happy to see 2 great grandchildren. Even at this age she wants to work and earn for herself and her family.</p>\r\n<h2>Medical Details</h2>\r\n<p>Initially she had a severe stomach ache with continuous flow of white discharge. She consulted a gynaecologist at Cambridge hospital, where she was examined and was diagnosed with the initial stages of cancer. She was referred to KIDWAI hospital where she underwent tests, 25 days of radiation and biopsy. During her treatment she had severe Diarrhea and white discharge and decided to stop the treatment at KIDWAI hospital because she couldn&rsquo;t bare the pain.</p>\r\n<p>Everything was fine and she returned to her normal routine, but one day she felt a sensation of a bubble bursting inside her stomach followed by vaginal bleeding. She consulted the same doctor in Cambridge hospital, on examination the doctor informed that the cancer had spread and she had to restart the treatment immediately. After that she came to HCG Hospital and took the opinion of a medical oncologist and a surgical oncologist. The doctors suggested surgery and 3 cycles of chemotherapy.</p>\r\n<p>As per the Doctors&rsquo; instructions she underwent surgery for stenting and currently she is receiving chemotherapy treatment.</p>\r\n<h2>Recent Update</h2>\r\n<p>Sarojamma has successfully completed her surgery and chemotherpay. She is doing well and has gone back to work, that is selling flowers.</p>','<p>Sarojamma, a 75-year-old hardworking woman, sells flowers near Sai Baba Temple in Indiranagar. She is blessed with three sons, a daughter, eight grandchildren and two great grandchildren.</p>','Sarojamma','Sarojamma','','2024-07-31 14:06:13'),
	(5,'Ammar Ahmed','ammar-ahmed','ammar-iamge_66a9f7e160441.jpg','Thursday, 2 April, 2020','NA','<h2>About Ammar</h2>\r\n<p>Ammar is a child who enjoys playing with his toys and is &ldquo;The Apple of my Eye&rdquo;, to both his mother and his father. This toddler is all of 2 years, very active and enthusiastic.</p>\r\n<p>He loves spending time with his family, by going out to the park along with his parents and his elder brother. A family of four hailing from Udupi and having settled in Saudi Arabia, his life is already filled with beautiful experiences. Now the family currently resides in Bangalore.</p>\r\n<h2>Medical Details</h2>\r\n<p>Ammar&rsquo;s symptoms started with persistent fever. The parents consulted a pediatrician in Saudi who suggested that the child be admitted in hospital for few days. Even after hospitalisation the fever didn&rsquo;t subside. After certain tests the child was diagnosed with leukaemia on 14th July 2019.</p>\r\n<p>The family flew down to India for his treatment and consulted Dr.Intezar Mehdi at HCG and understood the line of treatment. After MRI scan and blood tests, 5 cycles of chemotherapy was suggested. On 27 Jan 2020 Ammar has completed his chemotherapy and is on road to recovery .He is been advised maintenance chemotherapy for 2 years.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Case :</strong> Acute lymphoblastic leukaemia is the most common childhood cancer. It occurs when a bone marrow cell develops errors in its DNA. Symptoms may include enlarged lymph nodes, bruising, fever, bone pain, bleeding from the gums and frequent infections.</p>\r\n<p>The estimation for 5 cycles of chemotherapy was; 15-Lakhs. They have already spent around; 13-Lakhs for both chemotherapy and supportive care.</p>\r\n<h2>Recent Update</h2>\r\n<p>The family required financial aid for maintenance chemotherapy for 2 years: 1.25 lakhs. With the support from HCG Foundation and other donors Ammar completed his chemotherapy and went back to his hometown Mangalore.</p>','<p>Ammar is a child who enjoys playing with his toys and is &ldquo;The Apple of my Eye&rdquo;, to both his mother and his father. This toddler is all of 2 years, very active and enthusiastic.</p>','Ammar Ahmed','Ammar Ahmed','','2024-07-31 14:07:53'),
	(6,'Venkatesh V','venkatesh-v','venkatesh-image_66b1fd71b3d3b.jpg','Thursday, 2 April, 2020','Inactive','<h2>About Venkatesh</h2>\r\n<p>Venkatesh. V, is 49-years old and currently resides in JP Nagar, along with his wife Shantha. When he was 9 years old, Venkatesh lost his father due to Diabetes; the shock of losing her beloved husband was so devastating that, a few days later even his mother passed away. Leaving the children behind with a huge responsibility of paying back a family loan! Venkatesh began working a short while after in his relative&rsquo;s house till he was able to finish his 10th grade. Further to completing his 10th, he started working at Prakash Road Lines, as an office assistant, which he had to give up eventually because of personal commitments. In 1997, he was married off to Shantha, from a struggling lower-caste family and has been married ever since.</p>\r\n<p>The couple have no children; Venkatesh and Shantha are currently taking care of their relatives. Despite suffering from diabetes, high blood-pressure and thyroid; Shantha spends most of her time looking after an elder lady in the house, while Venkatesh manages small errands for the family in exchange for food and shelter.</p>\r\n<p>Venkatesh and Shantha dream of one day having their own home and a good meal amidst all of the situations they face.</p>\r\n<h2>Medical Details</h2>\r\n<p>In 2001, the patient vomited blood and also noticed blood in the sputum. He consulted a physician who advised certain tests along with a CBC. The results showed that he had CML cancer. Post which the patient was referred to KIDWAI. After the initial consultation at KIDWAI, there was a delay in carrying out the treatment. The concerned family, who were aware of HCG consulted Dr. Ravi Diwakar. Dr. Diwakar did a thorough analysis and suggested specific lab tests and procedures. Based on the test results the patient was put under medication.</p>\r\n<p>From 2005 the patient&rsquo;s condition has improved vastly and is on a bi-monthly check up plan.</p>\r\n<h2>Recent Update</h2>\r\n<p>Venkatesh, has successfully completed his treatment and is on his follow-up consultation. This was possible by the means of your contributions and support from HCG Foundation.</p>','<p>Venkatesh.V is 49-years old and currently resides in JP Nagar, along with his wife Shantha. When he was 9 years old, Venkatesh lost his father due to Diabetes.</p>','Venkatesh V','Venkatesh.V is 49-years old and currently resides in JP Nagar, along with his wife Shantha. When he was 9 years old, Venkatesh lost his father due to Diabetes.','','2024-08-06 16:09:45'),
	(7,'Prajwal','prajwal','prajwal_66b1fe1d0d009.png','Monday, 27 July, 2020','Inactive','<h2>About Prajwal</h2>\r\n<p>Prajwal is part of a family of four that resides in Bangalore, he is currently studying in a school near KR Puram along with his younger brother. His father is a contractor who provides labour for construction sites, while his mother is a home maker.</p>\r\n<p>He is currently in 4th std and is very studious and one day hopes to be an engineer. During his free time Prajwal loves playing cricket with his friends and spending time with family, especially his younger brother who he is very fond of.</p>\r\n<h2>Medical Details</h2>\r\n<p>In August 2019 last year his parents noticed that he was beginning to lose interest in everything he did. Prajwal had begun complaining about a repeated pain in his stomach, this made it hard for him to concentrate on studying and the reason for him showing a lack of interest in daily activities. Concerned about his well-being, his parents decided to get an MRI Scan done at Clumax Hospital, post which the Doctor advised them to go to Philomena Hospital.</p>\r\n<p>The presence of Wilm&rsquo;s tumor was confirmed post which they approached HCG Hospital where he began his treatment, after a thorough analysis of his report. The family was informed about the procedure &ndash; requiring Prajwal to undergo chemotherapy for 6-weeks along with surgery and has been advised to undergo further radiation treatment.</p>\r\n<h2>Recent Update</h2>\r\n<p>Prajwal, has successfully completed his treatment and is on his follow-up consultation. This was possible by the means of your contributions and support from HCG Foundation.</p>','<p>Prajwal is part of a family of four that resides in Bangalore, he is currently studying in a school near KR Puram along with his younger brother.</p>','Prajwal','Prajwal is part of a family of four that resides in Bangalore, he is currently studying in a school near KR Puram along with his younger brother.','','2024-08-06 16:12:37'),
	(8,'Jatin','jatin','jatin-image_66b1fe9812c73.jpg','Monday, 3 August, 2020','Inactive','<h2>About Jatin</h2>\r\n<p>Jatin is a 3-year old boy who stays in a joint family in Rajasthan. His father Manish, works at a hardware store as a service technician, while his mother is a homemaker. Jatin is a very active child who loves reading, studying and playing with his cousins at home.</p>\r\n<h2>Medical Details</h2>\r\n<p>In June 2020, on a sunny day while Jatin was playing outside his grandfather&rsquo;s house in Bangalore; his grandfather noticed that Jatin&rsquo;s body had turned yellow. The family immediately took him to Shanbhag Hospital where he underwent a blood test, X-ray and MRI scan. After going through the reports doctor referred them to Ramaiah hospital for further diagnosis.</p>\r\n<p>At Ramaiah in HCG Oncology division, Jatin underwent the following tests: &ndash; Blood Test and a PET-CT scan. Post test results, he was diagnosed with Acute-Lymphoblastic-Leukemia for which the doctors advised that he has to undergo chemotherapy for a period of 2 to 3 months.</p>\r\n<h2>Recent Update</h2>\r\n<p>Jatin, has successfully completed his treatment and is on his follow-up consultation. This was possible by the means of your contributions and support from HCG Foundation.</p>','Jatin is a 3-year old boy who stays in a joint family in Rajasthan. His father Manish, works at a hardware store as a service technician, while his mother is a homemaker.','Jatin','Jatin is a 3-year old boy who stays in a joint family in Rajasthan. His father Manish, works at a hardware store as a service technician, while his mother is a homemaker.','','2024-08-06 16:14:40'),
	(9,'Kamala','kamala','kamala-image_66b2006eae6b2.png','Monday, 17 August, 2020','Inactive','<h2>About Kamala</h2>\r\n<p>Kamala is 60-years old, currently residing in Sonnenahalli, Bangalore South; with her sister and grand-daughter. The family originally hails from Tamil-Nadu. Kamala used to work as a housekeeper and had decided not to get married as she wanted to take care of her parents.</p>\r\n<h2>Medical Details</h2>\r\n<p>Last year during a relatives wedding Kamala had an accident in the kitchen that hurt her breast region, which created a blood clot. She began experiencing pain on and off, although the pain had reduced, the blood clot grew into a lump over time. On June 7th- 2020, while she was sleeping the lump opened up and began bleeding.</p>\r\n<p>Her family immediately took her to Amar Jyothi Hospital, where she underwent a Mammogram, X-Ray and a Blood test.</p>\r\n<p>On seeing the reports the doctor informed that she has breast cancer and has to undergo immediate surgery.After a week Kamala underwent surgery to remove the tumour. She was referred for chemotherapy at HCG Hospital, where Dr. Vinayak informed her to undergo 4 cycles of chemotherapy. At present she has completed one cycle of chemotherapy and is yet to complete all her sessions.</p>\r\n<h2>Recent Update</h2>\r\n<p>Kamala has successfully completed her treatment and is on her follow-up consultation. This was possible by the means of your contributions and support from HCG Foundation.</p>','Kamala is 60-years old, currently residing in Sonnenahalli, Bangalore South; with her sister and grand-daughter. The family originally hails from Tamil-Nadu.','Kamala','Kamala is 60-years old, currently residing in Sonnenahalli, Bangalore South; with her sister and grand-daughter. The family originally hails from Tamil-Nadu.','','2024-08-06 16:22:30'),
	(10,'Aisha','kisha','aisha-image_66b2010ac9f9c.jpg','Thursday, 20 August, 2020','Inactive','<h2>About Aisha</h2>\r\n<p>Aisha is a 7-year old girl and is the oldest of two siblings a 3-year old brother and a 3-month old sister, in a household of five members. The family hails from Sirsi, where her father is a farmer and mother a home-maker. Aisha is an enthusiastic child who loves playing sports and participating in dance competitions at her school.</p>\r\n<h2>Medical Details</h2>\r\n<p>In 2019, during her summer vacation Aisha started complaining about a pain in her leg, for which they consulted a physician who prescribed medication for the same. However, after a few days while she was playing she experienced the pain again and it didn&rsquo;t subside.</p>\r\n<p>Concerned about her situation the family took her to TSS Hospital in Sirsi where she underwent a MRI Scan, the report showed the presence of cancer (Ewing Sarcoma). Based on the report, the doctors in Sirsi advised the family that she undergo treatment at KMC Hospital Mangalore. At KMC Hospital, post consultation and understanding the line of treatment, Aisha underwent 9-cycles of chemotherapy and later a Limb Salvage surgery at HCG Hospital.</p>\r\n<h2>Recent Update</h2>\r\n<p>Aisha has completed her surgery at HCG Hospital, under the supervision of Pediatric Oncologist Dr.Pramod. She is currently undergoing her chemotherapy at a hospital in Mangalore and is responding very well to the treatment.</p>','Aisha is a 7-year old girl and is the oldest of two siblings a 3-year old brother and a 3-month old sister, in a household of five members.','Aisha','Aisha is a 7-year old girl and is the oldest of two siblings a 3-year old brother and a 3-month old sister, in a household of five members.','','2024-08-06 16:25:06'),
	(11,'Ankita Basavaraj','ankita-basavaraj','ankita-bharadwaj-image_66b201917fcea.png','Thursday, 20 August, 2020','Inactive','<h2>About Ankita</h2>\r\n<p>Ankita is a 16-year old teenager who lives with her family in Belgaum,Karnataka. She is the eldest out of the four children, two brothers and a younger sister who all study in Cambridge School, Belgaum. Her father is a farmer, while the mother takes care of the house.</p>\r\n<p>At home, Ankita spends time with her siblings discussing various topics, interests and sharing stories. She loves practicing handwriting and studying science, with the aspiration to become a doctor one day to help people in need.</p>\r\n<h2>Medical Details</h2>\r\n<p>On 18th May 2018, Ankita started having recurring cases of fever, which despite her initial treatment at Alva&rsquo;s Hospital, Moodabidri; hadn&rsquo;t subsided. She was brought back to Belgaum where she diagnosed with acute lymphoblastic leukemia, post a blood test from a hospital.</p>\r\n<p>Moving ahead she was referred to HCG Hospital, where she began her course of chemotherapy and finished her maintenance chemotherapy session by 2019. During this period she developed a slight problem in her legs, making it hard for her to walk; for which she has been coming in for follow-up tests and treatment.</p>\r\n<h2>Recent Update</h2>\r\n<p>Ankita has completed her chemotherapy at HCG Hospital and is currently with her family in Belgaum. She has been going in for her follow up treatment under the supervision of Pediatric Oncologist Dr.Pramod.</p>','Ankita is a 16-year old teenager who lives with her family in Belgaum,Karnataka. She is the eldest out of the four children,','Ankita Basavaraj','Ankita is a 16-year old teenager who lives with her family in Belgaum,Karnataka. She is the eldest out of the four children,','','2024-08-06 16:27:21'),
	(12,'Anvitha','anvitha','anvitha-image_66b201fcf1b10.jpg','Thursday, 20 August, 2020','Inactive','<h2>About Anvitha</h2>\r\n<p>Anvitha is the only child and is treated as a princess in her family. The family resides in Bangalore, where her father is an engineer for a construction company and her mother, a homemaker. Being all of 2 years she loves spending time with her parents and occasionally plays with her toys and watches cartoons on TV.</p>\r\n<h2>Medical Details</h2>\r\n<p>Being an active toddler, Anvitha started to complain of stomach pain and developed fever. Her parents noticed that there was a slight swelling in the abdomen region. They immediately took her to a paediatrician who suggested: &ndash; Ultrasound Scan and CBC, post the tests Anvitha was diagnosed with Neuroblastoma Stage 4.The doctor advised, that she be treated at a specialised cancer hospital. A family friend suggested HCG Hospital, where they consulted with Dr.Intezar.</p>\r\n<p>She has undergone 4 types of treatment, that is; 8 cycles of chemotherapy, as continuation of treatment at a later stage she underwent surgery, BMT and radiation to stop the growth of cancer cells. She is now better, showing a great response in terms of recovery and is on her follow up consultation.</p>\r\n<h2>Recent Update</h2>\r\n<p>Anvitha has completed her maintenance chemotherapy at HCG Hospital and has completely recovered, she is currently on her follow up sessions under the supervision of Pediatric Oncologist Dr.Intezar.</p>','<p>Anvitha is the only child and is treated as a princess in her family. The family resides in Bangalore,</p>','Anvitha','Anvitha is the only child and is treated as a princess in her family. The family resides in Bangalore,','','2024-08-06 16:28:52'),
	(13,'Arpith','arpith','arpith-image_66b202b9e401f.jpg','Thursday, 20 August, 2020','Inactive','<h2>About Arpith</h2>\r\n<p>Arpith is a 14-year old boy studying in 10th std in a government and is very intelligent when it comes to his studies. He stays in a family of five, his father is a security guard and mother a home maker. He has an elder sister and a brother. He loves dancing and has performed in a couple of shows in Mangalore. He aspires to get a job in the banking sector, after his education.</p>\r\n<h2>Medical Details</h2>\r\n<p>In October 2018, Arpith noticed a small lump near his right knee. The family consulted an orthopaedic near their home, post the tests the X-Ray showed the presence of a small tumour in his knee. The doctor further advised the family to get a CT scan and Blood test done for him. This was the final confirmation on the presence of a tumour and the method of treatment was explained to the family.</p>\r\n<p>Since the family could not afford the cost of treatment, they got Arpith treated for 3-months by an Ayurvedic doctor. However, the treatment had only alleviated the pain and the size of the tumour. Concerned, the family took him in for a second consultation and a scan with an orthopaedic in Mangalore and the results revealed that the tumour had become malignant.</p>\r\n<p>Moving ahead the family was referred to HCG Hospital, Bengaluru; where they consulted Dr.Pramod. After getting the biopsy report Arpith had to undergo 4-cycles of chemotherapy to remove and dissolve any lasting traces of the tumour making sure it does not recur.</p>\r\n<p>The family has gone back to Mangalore where, Arpith is currently going for his physiotherapy sessions under the supervision and consultation of Dr.Pramod&rsquo;s team.</p>\r\n<h2>Recent Update</h2>\r\n<p>Arpith, recently consulted with a Doctor. It is suspected that there might be a, &lsquo;Reoccurrence&rsquo;. His results are awaited.</p>','Arpith is a 14-year old boy studying in 10th std in a government and is very intelligent when it comes to his studies.','Arpith','Arpith is a 14-year old boy studying in 10th std in a government and is very intelligent when it comes to his studies.','','2024-08-06 16:32:17'),
	(14,'Moksha Jain','moksha-jain','moksha-jain-image_66b2033d86b2d.jpg','Thursday, 20 August, 2020','Inactive','<h2>About Moksha Jain</h2>\r\n<p>Moksha, is a 11 year old girl who stays with her family, she is the oldest out of the two children and is very close to her younger brother. Her mother works as an LIC agent and her father is a pygmy collector. The family lives in Mudbidri, Karnataka. She is a very active girl and loves dancing, especially her love for Bharatanatyam, she has completed her junior level in Bharatanatyam and also holds a black belt in Karate. In her free time she enjoys skating.</p>\r\n<h2>Medical Details</h2>\r\n<p>Moksha initially complained about a slight pain in her leg which gradually increased over time, even after basic medication. In due course, she developed a lump in her leg, for which she had to undergo various tests: &ndash; X-Ray, CT scan and blood tests were conducted by an Orthopaedic in Mudbidri.</p>\r\n<p>The family was then suggested to meet Dr.Pramod at HCG Hospital, where she underwent a PET Scan and Biopsy. The reports showed the presence of Osteosarcoma, which had grown over the previous few months. Moksha underwent a few cycles of chemotherapy and surgery to remove tumour and is currently doing better.</p>\r\n<h2>Recent Update</h2>\r\n<p>Moksha Jain underwent surgery at HCG Hospital, under the supervision of Dr.Pramod. She is currently undergoing her chemotherapy sessions at a hospital in Mudbidri and is responding positively to the treatment.</p>','Moksha, is a 11 year old girl who stays with her family, she is the oldest out of the two children and is very close to her younger brother.','Moksha Jain','Moksha, is a 11 year old girl who stays with her family, she is the oldest out of the two children and is very close to her younger brother.','','2024-08-06 16:34:29'),
	(15,'Amala','amala','amala-image_66b203b4e0dde.jpg','Monday, 24 August, 2020','Inactive','<h2>About Amala</h2>\r\n<p>Amala is a 67-year old lady staying with her three children, the family is originally from Tamil-Nadu and are currently staying in Kammanahalli, Bengaluru. Her husband expired 10-years back; her eldest son Peter works as a helper in a carpenter shop, her younger son Anthony is a Sales-executive at a clothing store and her daughter who is married works as a Beautician. Amala loves spending time with her children and in her free time enjoys watching films.</p>\r\n<h2>Medical Details</h2>\r\n<p>In April 2020, Amala started experiencing pain in her right breast and felt a lump that had increased in size. Her family initially took her to Silver Line Hospital in Kammanahalli, where she was asked to get an X-Ray and FNAC test. As they did not have the facility to conduct the tests, they were referred to Specialist Hospital, where Amala was able to get the FNAC test done, post which she was diagnosed with Carcinoma in her right breast.</p>\r\n<p>A family friend then asked the family to visit HCG Hospital, Bengaluru. At HCG Hospital, they consulted Dr.Jaganath Dixit, after seeing the reports she underwent a Mammogram and Biopsy. The next step was for her to undergo surgery conducted by Dr. Jaganath. The lump was removed and sent in for testing. Post the test results, Amala has to undergo 8-cycles of Chemotherapy and Radiotherapy.</p>\r\n<h2>Recent Update</h2>\r\n<p>Amala, has successfully completed her treatment and is on her follow-up consultation. This was possible by the means of your contributions and support from HCG Foundation.</p>','Amala is a 67-year old lady staying with her three children, the family is originally from Tamil-Nadu and are currently staying in Kammanahalli, Bengaluru.','Amala','Amala is a 67-year old lady staying with her three children, the family is originally from Tamil-Nadu and are currently staying in Kammanahalli, Bengaluru.','','2024-08-06 16:36:28'),
	(16,'Suvarna','suvarna','suvarna-image_66b2040d31461.jpg','Monday, 24 August, 2020','Inactive','<h2>About Suvarna</h2>\r\n<p>Suvarna is a 10-year old girl who stays with her family in H.D Kote, Mysore. Her father works as a daily wage worker and her mother takes up coolie work from time to time. Suvarna is a very active girl studying in 3rd STD in a government school along with her brother who is 2nd STD. She loves spending her time studying, reading and playing with her friends.</p>\r\n<h2>Medical Details</h2>\r\n<p>In June 2019, she began complaining about a pain in her neck, this pain was caused by the presence of a lump which was also the main culprit for her recurring and persistent fever. The family took her to KR Hospital where she underwent a biopsy. Post the test-results, she was diagnosed with Non-Hodgkin&rsquo;s Lymphoma. The Doctor in KR Hospital referred them to a hospital in Bengaluru, as this was inconvenient to the family, they approached Bharath Cancer HCG Hospital, Mysuru.</p>\r\n<p>At Bharath Cancer HCG Hospital, she underwent a CT-Scan, Blood test and surgery to treat the lump. Suvarna, now has to undergo 8-cycles of Chemotherapy.</p>\r\n<h2>Current Update</h2>\r\n<p>It is with a heavy heart that we share this update with you. Our cancer-fighter Suvarna is no longer with us! We convey our prayers and deepest condolences to her family. May she rest-in-peace!</p>','Suvarna is a 10-year old girl who stays with her family in H.D Kote, Mysore. Her father works as a daily wage worker and her mother takes up coolie work from time to time.','Suvarna','Suvarna is a 10-year old girl who stays with her family in H.D Kote, Mysore. Her father works as a daily wage worker and her mother takes up coolie work from time to time.','','2024-08-06 16:37:57'),
	(17,'Bharathbhai','bharathbhai','bharathbhai-image_66b2047f74cf1.jpg','Wednesday, 26 August, 2020','Inactive','<h2>About Bharathbhai</h2>\r\n<p>Bharatbhai is 40 yrs old, currently residing in Porbandar, Gujarat. He stays with his wife and two daughters (6 yrs &amp; 2.5 yrs respectively) in a rented house. He himself is working as a driver in courier line company since last 3 yrs and earning Rs 6000 per month.</p>\r\n<h2>Medical Details</h2>\r\n<p>Was operated earlier this year in Feb 2020, and after that was not working because of surgery and lockdown. Had started going to work since last one month, but again has got cancer and needs to undergo small surgery.</p>\r\n<p>Bharatbhai, had got pain in his mouth early this year and one of his relative who was operated in HCG; referred him to HCG, Ahmedabad. Patient was diagnosed with CA right buccal mucosa and was operated for the same in Feb 2020.</p>\r\n<p>After 6 months, he has been diagnosed with left cervical metastatic node and needs to undergo a small surgery.</p>\r\n<h2>Financial Details</h2>\r\n<p>He has spent 2-Lakhs for his pervious surgery, by borrowing money from his friends and relatives, who have supported him.</p>\r\n<p>At the moment he has exhausted all his resources and needs Rs 1,60,000/- for his 2nd surgery.</p>\r\n<h2>Required Aid</h2>\r\n<p>Bharatbhai needs a financial aid of Rs 1,60,000 for his 2nd surgery.</p>\r\n<h5>Total Fundraising Goal: INR 1,60,000</h5>','Bharatbhai is 40 yrs old, currently residing in Porbandar, Gujarat. He stays with his wife and two daughters','Bharathbhai','Bharatbhai is 40 yrs old, currently residing in Porbandar, Gujarat. He stays with his wife and two daughters','','2024-08-06 16:39:51'),
	(18,'Harini M','harini-m','harini-m-image_66b2050c75c57.jpg','Thursday, 3 September, 2020','Inactive','<h2>About Harini</h2>\r\n<p>Harini is a 12-year old school going child studying in 6th grade at Lawrence High school. She is the only child and stays with her family in Bengaluru. She loves spending time with her maternal grandmother and enjoys reading books, as english is her favourite subject. In her free time, Harini loves playing badminton, cycling classical dance, music and watching cartoons. Her dream is to become a Doctor after her education.</p>\r\n<h2>Medical Details</h2>\r\n<p>Initially would get recurring fever and slowly started developing red coloured patches on her body. Concerned about this development, she was taken to a general pediatrician. After undergoing certain blood tests the family was informed that her platelets are too low and they had to be treated. Later, she got a bone marrow test done and was diagnosed with; ALL &ndash; B cell stage-1(Acute Lymphoblastic Leukemia) and referred to HCG Hospital.</p>\r\n<p>At HCG Hospital; the family consulted Dr. Intezar, after going through reports and her condition suggested a 45 day &lsquo;hospitalization&rsquo;. Her treatment of chemotherapy started from April 2017 till 2019 May end. Up-till now she has finished 3-cycles of chemotherapy along with blood investigation and 5-cycles of maintenance chemotherapy.</p>\r\n<h2>Recent Update</h2>\r\n<p>Harini has completely recovered is currently on her follow-up consultations and undergoing blood investigations.</p>','Harini is a 12-year old school going child studying in 6th grade at Lawrence High school. She is the only child and stays with her family in Bengaluru.','Harini M','Harini is a 12-year old school going child studying in 6th grade at Lawrence High school. She is the only child and stays with her family in Bengaluru.','','2024-08-06 16:42:12'),
	(19,'Hethashree','hethashree','hethashree-image_66b2057d2ff84.jpg','Thursday, 3 September, 2020','Inactive','<h2>About Hethashree</h2>\r\n<p>Hethashree, is a 14-year old teenager who lives with her family of 4-members including her Parents and a younger brother(11-years old). Her mother is a house wife and father is an account manager at a construction company, 9 -months back he had a brain-stroke due to which he had to stop working.</p>\r\n<p>Hethashree is studying in 8th Std, along with her younger brother who is in 4th Std at Louis High School. She is very active when it comes to sports activities and is a track-runner at her school. She loves spending time with her family at home and in her free time enjoys listening to music.</p>\r\n<h2>Medical Details</h2>\r\n<p>In January 2020, she started having pain in her legs, hence; her parents took her to a physician near Nandini Layout. She was administered with painkillers which weren&rsquo;t effective in easing the pain. Gradually over the next few months she had developed a lump in her leg. Concerned about this, her family took her to &lsquo;Fortis Hospital&rsquo;, where she underwent an MRI-Scan . The orthopaedic confirmed the presence of &lsquo;Osteosarcoma&rsquo; and referred the family to HCG Hospital.</p>\r\n<p>At HCG Hospital, they consulted Dr. Pramod. Hethashree got a PET-CT Scan and Biopsy done, post which she underwent 2-cycles chemotherapy and surgery. April 1st, 2020 was when she started her first cycle of chemotherapy along with a chemo-port-insertion. She is yet to undergo four more admissions of chemotherapy and two surgeries</p>\r\n<h2>Recent Update</h2>\r\n<p>Hethashree has completed her treatment.</p>','Hethashree, is a 14-year old teenager who lives with her family of 4-members including her Parents and a younger brother(11-years old).','Hethashree','Hethashree, is a 14-year old teenager who lives with her family of 4-members including her Parents and a younger brother(11-years old).','','2024-08-06 16:44:05'),
	(20,'Mudassir','mudassir','mudassir-image_66b205e6d2a45.jpg','Thursday, 3 September, 2020','Inactive','<h2>About Mudassir</h2>\r\n<p>Mudassir, is a 16-year old teenage boy who stays in household of 5-members, his parents and two younger sister&rsquo;s 9-year old Madiha and 7-year old Misbah. His father is an Arabic teacher in a Mosque and his mother Mohsia is a homemaker.</p>\r\n<p>Mudassir is a smart, enthusiastic and responsible child who looks up to his parents. When taking a break from his daily activities, he loves drawing and playing games with his siblings</p>\r\n<h2>Medical Details</h2>\r\n<p>In the month of December(2019), a swelling had developed in Mudassir&rsquo;s neck, that began growing in size and became painful to touch. The first time around the Doctor&rsquo;s hinted that the reason for the swelling could be because of winter season in Bengaluru. However, over the next few days the swelling started interfering with his normal activities such as :- eating, drinking and even speaking.</p>\r\n<p>The family took him to a hospital where certain tests were done, post which; it was confirmed that the swelling was cancerous. He was then referred to HCG Hospital, where he met Dr. Intezar .After getting blood tests and scans done, the report revealed the presence of Hodgkin Lymphoma Stage 3. The method of treatment was explained to the family, and Mudassir began his Induction chemotherapy sessions. He has completed his initial treatment, he is on his follow up consultations, under investigation and is yet to undergo the final stage of treatment.</p>\r\n<p>Mudassir requires financial aid of 2-lakhs for his follow-up consultation, investigation and treatment.</p>\r\n<h2>Recent Update</h2>\r\n<p>Mudassir has successfully completed his treatment, he is currently studying in 9th STD and is living happily with his family. He is on regular follow-up with a pediatric oncologist.</p>','Mudassir, is a 16-year old teenage boy who stays in household of 5-members, his parents and two younger sisterâ€™s 9-year old Madiha and 7-year old','Mudassir','Mudassir, is a 16-year old teenage boy who stays in household of 5-members, his parents and two younger sisterâ€™s 9-year old Madiha and 7-year old','','2024-08-06 16:45:50'),
	(21,'Navdeep Reddy','navdeep-reddy','navdeep-reddy-image_66b2064c2315f.jpg','Thursday, 3 September, 2020','Inactive','<h2>About Navdeep Reddy</h2>\r\n<p>Navdeep is a 15-year old teenage boy who stays in a household of 4-members, his parents and ayounger brother. The family hail from Chittoor,Andhra Pradesh. Navdeep is studying in 9th Std. His father Chandrasekhar is a farmer, mother a home maker and younger brother is in 5th Std. Navdeep is a hardworking and studious boy who aspires to become an IAS officer. During his free time he enjoys playing cricket and watching adventurous movies.</p>\r\n<h2>Medical Details</h2>\r\n<p>In July 2018, Navdeep came home limping as he had hurt himself while playing. The pain was persistent and wasn&rsquo;t subsiding, concerned about this his family took him to a Hospital. After getting an X-ray, the report showed the presence of a tumor in his leg. To be certain about the diagnosis, the family took Navdeep to Ambedkar Hospital where it was confirmed that he had Osteosarcoma.</p>\r\n<p>The family was referred to HCG Hospital, where Navdeep got a round of tests and a biopsy done. He was then advised to undergo 3-cycles of chemotherapy and surgery to remove the tumor; post which, he underwent another 3-cycles of chemotherapy.</p>\r\n<h2>Recent Update</h2>\r\n<p>Navdeep has completed his surgery and chemotherapy, he is currently on his regular follow-up consultations with HCG Hospital, under Dr.Pramod. Navdeep has resumed his schooling (9th Std) back in Chittoor, Andhra Pradesh.</p>','Navdeep is a 15-year old teenage boy who stays in a household of 4-members, his parents and ayounger brother.','Navdeep Reddy','Navdeep is a 15-year old teenage boy who stays in a household of 4-members, his parents and ayounger brother.','','2024-08-06 16:47:32'),
	(22,'Rida','rida','rida-image_66b206f7c5efa.jpg','Thursday, 3 September, 2020','Inactive','<h2>About Rida</h2>\r\n<p>Rida, is an 8-year old girl studying in 1st Std, belongs to a family of four that includes her parents and a younger sister. The family is from Bengaluru and currently residing in R.T. Nagar. Her father is a technician in a lab and her mother is a teacher in a private school. Rida, loves going to school, spending time with her family and enjoys playing games with her younger sister.</p>\r\n<h2>Medical Details</h2>\r\n<p>In August 2017, Rida had fluctuating fever for approximately 4 weeks. As the antibiotics were not reducing her fever, her family got her CBC done in a diagnostic centre and consulted a pediatrist with the report. The doctor referred them to HCG Hospital, where Rida underwent a CBC and a Bone Marrow test. On 28th October 2017 she was diagnosed with, Acute-Lymphoblastic-Leukemia and the family was briefed about the line of treatment. The doctor started her chemotherapy in the month of December, which continued for a year. She also underwent her maintenance chemotherapy and is on her follow-up consultations.</p>\r\n<h2>Recent Update</h2>\r\n<p>Rida has completed her chemotherapy and is back to her normal life. She is studying in 1st Std at a school in R.T. Nagar. She is also on her regular follow-up consultations.</p>','Rida, is an 8-year old girl studying in 1st Std, belongs to a family of four that includes her parents and a younger sister.','Rida','Rida, is an 8-year old girl studying in 1st Std, belongs to a family of four that includes her parents and a younger sister.','','2024-08-06 16:50:23'),
	(23,'Falguni','falguni','falguni-image_66badcd5e18fe.jpg','Sunday, 3 September, 2020','Inactive','<h2>About Falguni</h2>\r\n<p>Falguni is a 42-year old woman staying with her family in Jamshedpur. She has two daughters; one is studying in 10th Grade and the other is doing her graduate studies. Her husband is into the automobile business in Jamshedpur and Falguni manages the household. She loves spending time with her family.</p>\r\n<h2>Medical Details</h2>\r\n<p>In 2014, she started experiencing pain in her abdomen, concerned; her family took her to Fortis Hospital in Kolkata. After getting a scan done, the Doctors found the presence of a tumor in her colon. She underwent a uterus removal surgery, which was then sent in for a biopsy. The Doctor on seeing the biopsy report mentioned that the tumor was cancerous. She was advised to under-go 8-cycles of chemotherapy at Tata Hospital in Kolkata, post which she recovered completely.</p>\r\n<p>A few years later in 2017, on her follow-up consultations with the Doctor, they found the presence of a tumor in her uterus. She had to undergo another tumor removal surgery which was successful. In the beginning of 2020, Falguni was diagnosed with Lung-Carcinoma. She underwent 21-admissions of chemotherapy and was put under medication, as the medication didn&rsquo;t respond with her body she was put under palliative care. In March 2020, she started experiencing severe breathlessness; due to the lockdown she had to stay home. The family brought her to HCG Hospital, Bengaluru in August where she underwent one cycle of chemotherapy and immunotherapy. She is yet to undergo further treatment along the same line.</p>\r\n<h2>Recent Update</h2>\r\n<p>By the means of your contributions and support from HCG Foundation, Falguni has completed her treatment and is on her follow-up consultations.</p>','<p>Falguni is a 42-year old woman staying with her family in Jamshedpur. She has two daughters; one is studying in 10th Grade and the other is</p>','Falguni','Falguni is a 42-year old woman staying with her family in Jamshedpur. She has two daughters; one is studying in 10th Grade and the other is','','2024-08-13 09:41:01'),
	(24,'Kapilaben Gurja','kapilaben-gurja','kapilaben-gurja_66badda74e7df.png','Sunday, 3 September, 2020','Inactive','<h2>About Kapilaben Gurja</h2>\r\n<p>Kapilaben, is 48-years old residing in Ahmedabad, Gujarat. She stays with her husband, mother in law and two children (daughter &amp; son). They stay in a two room and kitchen house which was originally given to them by their elders.</p>\r\n<p>Her husband is working with a Bank and earns Rs 35,000/- per month. Their daughter has been engaged for the last 2-years, due to her mother&rsquo;s medical condition her marriage has been put on hold. He has almost spent almost all money from his Provident Fund account.</p>\r\n<h2>Medical Details</h2>\r\n<p>Patient has been suffering from an orthopaedic problem since the last 28 years and has already been operated on six times. The family has spent around 15 -20 lakhs, till date for her treatment. Recently in May 2020, she underwent a hip-replacement operation for which they spent around 4.5 Lakhs. The family had to spend money on the surgery by selling off their daughter&rsquo;s marriage gold</p>\r\n<p>Kapilaben, is bed ridden since the last 6-months and is immobile. The family consulted Dr Dipak Dave and Dr Jyotindra Pandit, where-in they suggested the further mode of treatment. After having a look at the reports, they found that Kapilaben had developed an infection for which she needs to undergo another surgery.</p>\r\n<h2>Recent Update</h2>\r\n<p>Kapilaben, has completed her treatment and is on her follow-up consultations.</p>','<p>Kapilaben, is 48-years old residing in Ahmedabad, Gujarat. She stays with her husband, mother in law and two children</p>','Kapilaben Gurja','Kapilaben, is 48-years old residing in Ahmedabad, Gujarat. She stays with her husband, mother in law and two children','','2024-08-13 09:44:31'),
	(25,'Princy','princy','princy-image_66bade15e786b.jpg','Monday, 11 September, 2020','Inactive','<h2>About Princy</h2>\r\n<p>Princy Khalkho is an 8-year old girl, the only child to her parents Mr.Pradeep Bhagat and Mrs.Basanthi Gara. The family is from Ranchi, Jharkand staying in their own home. Her father works as a security guard and earning a meagre 10,000/- INR a month; while her mother is a cook at a Blind School.</p>\r\n<p>Princy is studying in 3rd STD at Kendriya Vidyalaya, she is an enthusiastic and studious; who is focused on her academics.</p>\r\n<h2>Medical Details</h2>\r\n<p>When Princy was 6-months old, she had developed a lump in her hip that started growing. Concerned about this development, her parents took her to a Hospital in Ranchi. At the hospital, she underwent a few blood tests and a FNAC test; post-report her parents were informed that there was the presence of cancer-cells and referred them to CMC Hospital, Vellore for further treatment. At CMC Hospital, Vellore; Princy underwent 6-cycles of chemotherapy along with radiation therapy and a surgery to remove the lump. After her surgery, she underwent another 2-cycles of chemotherapy treatment over a year, she responded well to the treatment and was cured. The family then returned to their native, while taking her for a yearly check-up at CMC, Vellore.</p>\r\n<p>Mr.Pradeep and Mrs.Basanthi &ndash; We have seen her go through the pain and suffering as a 6-month old baby; as parents it isn&rsquo;t easy to watch your only child fight a battle that she isn&rsquo;t familiar with. Watching her life hang in the balance, each day and night had grown longer for us; we just wanted to get out of this long dark tunnel. Nothing else mattered to us, we just wanted our baby girl to become better and healthy!</p>\r\n<p>Years later, in 2019 on one of her follow-ups; Princy was diagnosed with cancer. The very same spot in her hip, the cancerous-cells had recurred. The family is still paying-off the initial loan amount for her treatment and have exhausted all their savings. Upon their request, they were referred to HCG Hospital, Ranchi; which is closer to the family. She has begun her chemotherapy treatment and is yet to undergo 4-Cycles of chemotherapy and surgery; 2-cycles prior and 2-cycles post her surgery.</p>\r\n<p>A hopeful Pradeep and Basanthi, who had imagined that their daughter was healed; we are re-living our worst nightmares and memories of Princy&rsquo;s initial fight against Cancer as a 6-month old baby. It has been very stressful for us this year financially as we are still clearing the initial loan amount. We are now watching our child go through this suffering again and it is unbearable. Our only hope is that she recovers successfully and lives a beautiful life that is meant for her.</p>\r\n<h2>Update</h2>\r\n<p>Princy, has completed her treatment and she is on her regular follow-up consultations.</p>','<p>Princy Khalkho is an 8-year old girl, the only child to her parents Mr.Pradeep Bhagat and Mrs.Basanthi Gara. The family is from Ranchi, Jharkand staying in their own home.</p>','Princy','Princy Khalkho is an 8-year old girl, the only child to her parents Mr.Pradeep Bhagat and Mrs.Basanthi Gara. The family is from Ranchi, Jharkand staying in their own home.','','2024-08-13 09:46:21'),
	(26,'Uday Kiran','uday-kiran','uday-kiran-image_66badeb517f85.jpg','Wednesday, 16 September, 2020','Inactive','<h2>About Uday Kiran</h2>\r\n<p>Uday Kiran is a 17-year old teenager, who stays with his mother and aunt in Yelahanka Old Town, Bangalore. Uday&rsquo;s father expired when he was 1-year old. He is studying in 2nd PUC, Commerce; at a Government PU College. His mother works as tailor at a Garment shop.</p>\r\n<p>Uday wants to become a government employee post his studies, so that he can support and provide all facilities for his mother. Uday is a movie-buff and in his free time enjoys watching a good film, one of his most favourite role model is Actor Prabhas.</p>\r\n<h2>Medical Details</h2>\r\n<p>In 2017, Uday started experiencing headaches; over time it became persistent and these headaches wouldn&rsquo;t subside. Accompanied by his mother, he consulted a doctor near his house who prescribed some medication and suggested that he undergo a CT-Scan. The reports showed the presence of a lump in his brain. The family consulted doctors at ESI Hospital, who recommended that he get treated at HCG Hospital. At HCG under Dr.Mayur Uday, he underwent a surgery on 1st May 2018, to remove the lump in his brain. Post surgery he started having seizures, for which he was admitted on observation for the next 5-days.</p>\r\n<p>Later that year in November, he began experiencing headaches with increased intensity &amp; visual disturbances for which he was operated on. Post-surgery he was advised to undergo a MRI-Scan to assess his condition. Post-assessment it was confirmed that the lump had reoccured, a MRI-DOPA Scan was done to finalise the mode of treatment. Uday, then underwent radiotherapy to remove the lump.</p>\r\n<p>With financial support from HCG Foundation, the family was able to bear the costs of all the treatments</p>\r\n<h2>Recent Update</h2>\r\n<p>Uday Kiran has successfully completed his treatment and has recovered from this life threatening tumor. He is consistent in taking his medication and is couldn&rsquo;t be happier to be back home with his family. He has gone back to pursuing his 2nd PUC studies, resiliently focusing towards achieving his dream.</p>','Uday Kiran is a 17-year old teenager, who stays with his mother and aunt in Yelahanka Old Town, Bangalore.','Uday Kiran','Uday Kiran is a 17-year old teenager, who stays with his mother and aunt in Yelahanka Old Town, Bangalore.','','2024-08-13 09:49:01'),
	(27,'Mudassir Ahmed','mudassir-ahmed','mudassir-ahmed_66badf4a0ca1f.jpg','Wednesday, 16 September, 2020','Inactive','<h2>About Mudassir Ahmed</h2>\r\n<p>Mudassir Ahmed is joyful 4-year old child who stays in a joint family in Nagpur. His father Mr.Sohail Iqbal, used to work as a medical transcriptionist and his mother Mrs.Mehar is a home-maker.</p>\r\n<p>This is a family that is filled with love and positive energy, always supporting each other and spending their days sharing stories. Mudassir, loves spending time with his family and especially playing games with his cousins.</p>\r\n<h2>Medical Details</h2>\r\n<p>During the month of June 2019, Mudassir started having excruciating pain from his knees down till his toes and this pain would persist for a few hours. Initially, the family thought that he might have hurt himself while playing and took him to a pediatrician. The Doctor, upon examining him prescribed Vitamin-E medication thinking that the pain was caused due to deficiency. On noticing that his pain hadn&rsquo;t reduced over the weeks, the family took him to an Orthopedic. Mudassir, underwent a few blood-tests and the reports showed the presence of infection in his blood. The Doctor suspected it to be either blood or bone cancer and to get an accurate response referred the family to HCG Hospital, Nagpur.</p>\r\n<p>At HCG Hospital, he underwent specific blood tests and the reports confirmed the presence of B-CELL Acute Lymphoblastic Leukemia. The Doctors explained the line of treatment to the family post which, Mudassir underwent 6-cycles of chemotherapy. He is currently undergoing his maintenance chemotherapy.</p>\r\n<h2>Financial Details</h2>\r\n<p>The family has already spent approximately 10-Lakh for his treatment, by receiving support from family and friends. They also initiated a &lsquo;WhatsApp Campaign&rsquo;, for donations, from which they were able to cover the costs.</p>\r\n<p>They are currently struggling at the moment to arrange 3-Lakh for his maintenance chemotherapy and supportive care. In this challenging time, let&rsquo;s come together and financially support Mudassir.</p>\r\n<h2>Required Aid</h2>\r\n<p>Mudassir Ahmed, needs financial aid of &lsquo;3-Lakh&rsquo;, for his maintenance chemotherapy and supportive care.</p>\r\n<h2>Total Fundraising Goal: INR 3,00,000</h2>','Mudassir Ahmed is joyful 4-year old child who stays in a joint family in Nagpur. His father Mr.Sohail Iqbal, used to work as a medical transcriptionist','Mudassir Ahmed','Mudassir Ahmed is joyful 4-year old child who stays in a joint family in Nagpur. His father Mr.Sohail Iqbal, used to work as a medical transcriptionist','','2024-08-13 09:51:30'),
	(28,'Kalaiarasan','kalaiarasan','kalaiarasan-image_66badfbeca5a0.jpg','Thursday, 1 October, 2020','Inactive','<h2>About Kalaiarasan</h2>\r\n<p>Kalaiarasan is a 24-year old adult staying with his family; his parents, grandmother and two younger brothers in their own house in Krishnagiri, Tamilnadu. He is final year MBA student, studying at Perumal College, Hosur. His father runs a small-scale vehicle dealership, his mother is a homemaker and his younger brothers are pursuing their degree.</p>\r\n<p>Kalaiarasan, is an active Cricket enthusiast and loves playing cricket with his friends. When not playing his favorite sport, Kalaiarasan spends his time reading and studying. He is also a movie-buff, an ardent follower of the latest movies and enjoys sharing his points of view about them.</p>\r\n<h2>Medical Details</h2>\r\n<p>In August 2018, Kalaiarasan started feeling a numbness on the left side of his face and a blockage in his left nasal-tract. After consulting an ENT specialist near his home, post examination; the Doctor informed that there was a small flesh-growth in his nose and that he needed to undergo surgery. The family took him to Apollo Hospital, Chennai; for surgery, it was here once he underwent a biopsy that he was diagnosed with Nasopharyngeal-Carcinoma (NPC). The family consulted a Doctor at Manipal Hospital, to get a second opinion, where the cancer was re-confirmed. The family was informed about the line of treatment, post which; he began his treatment at Kumaran Hospital, Chennai. He underwent 7-cycles of chemotherapy and 3-cycles of maintenance chemotherapy along with radiation. After completing his treatment, he has been on his follow-up consultations once every three months and was doing well.</p>\r\n<p>In September 2020, on his follow-up consultation, he underwent a PET-CT Scan, where the report showed the presence of tumor in the same place. The Doctor suggested that he needed to undergo chemotherapy again to control the growth. This time, however; after suggestions from the family they approached HCG Hospital and consulted Dr.Srinivas. After doing the needed tests, Dr.Srinivas has suggested that he needs to undergo 8-cycles of chemotherapy and 5-cycles of immunotherapy.</p>\r\n<p>Parents Speak &ndash; Mr.Karuthappan and Mrs.Vijaya :- We had thought that he was completely cured, but when we got to know that the cancer had relapsed, our hearts sank. We have already spent all our savings for his first treatment and now we request you to kindly support us and help raise the amount required. You are our only hope at this moment!</p>\r\n<p>We cannot see our Son suffer once again to cancer and this time we pray and hope that he recovers successfully and is back to his enthusiastic self. We need your help, kindly donate as much as you can; so that we can pay for his treatment.</p>\r\n<p>Kalaiarasan, is currently undergoing his chemotherapy.</p>\r\n<h2>Financial Details</h2>\r\n<p>The family has already spent close to 10-lakhs for his initial treatment and have exhausted all their savings.</p>\r\n<p>The estimated cost for his further treatment is 15-lakhs, the family are in dire need of financial support and need your help during these challenging times.</p>\r\n<h2>Required Aid</h2>\r\n<p>Kalaiarasan requires financial aid of approximately 15-Lakhs, for his chemotherapy, immunotherapy and supportive care.</p>\r\n<h2>Total Fundraising Goal: INR 15,00,000</h2>','Kalaiarasan is a 24-year old adult staying with his family; his parents, grandmother and two younger brothers in their own house in Krishnagiri, Tamilnadu.','Kalaiarasan','Kalaiarasan is a 24-year old adult staying with his family; his parents, grandmother and two younger brothers in their own house in Krishnagiri, Tamilnadu.','','2024-08-13 09:53:26'),
	(29,'Zarine','zarine','zarine-image_66bae02514029.jpg','Tuesday, 6 October, 2020','Inactive','<h2>About Zarine</h2>\r\n<p>Zarine is a 10-year old girl, staying with her family in Nagpur. Her father Aslam is a farmer, her mother Ruksana is a house-wife, her elder sister is studying in 7th Std and Zarine studies in 5th Std. She is a child who loves dancing and also participating in painting competitions in school.</p>\r\n<h2>Medical Details</h2>\r\n<p>In 2020, she developed a fever which wouldn&rsquo;t subside, even after regular check-ups at a clinic. After consulting a family Doctor and as per his suggestion, she underwent a platelet test and the report showed that her platelet-count was low.</p>\r\n<p>Concerned about her well-being, the family visited HCG-Nagpur; where they consulted with Dr.Nishad. After going through the report and conducting a bone-marrow-test, she was diagnosed with Hemophagocytic-Lymphohistiocytosis (HLH). She has been advised to undergo a Bone-Marrow-Transplant. She is currently under supportive treatment at Lata Mangeshkar Hospital, Nagpur. Once her fever comes down, she will be undergoing a Bone-Marrow-Transplant.</p>\r\n<p>Parents Speak &ndash; Mr.Aslam and Mrs.Ruksana :- Our child was very active, she would paint and enjoy dancing. Now, she is bedridden and it breaks our hearts. At this point, watching her undergo so much pain has brought us to our knees; getting her fever stabilized is very challenging and she is in the ICU.</p>\r\n<p>Mr.Aslam &ndash; I am ready to sell my agricultural land as it is very challenging to arrange 30-Lakhs for her BMT- treatment, to me; my daughter is my whole world and nothing else matters. I just want her to get better and recover successfully! This is our only hope, wish and prayer for our child.</p>\r\n<p>Zarine, is currently undergoing her BMT treatment.</p>\r\n<h2>Financial Details</h2>\r\n<p>The family has already spent 3-Lakhs for her initial treatment and have exhausted their savings.</p>\r\n<p>The family needs 30-Lakhs for her BMT-treatment and supportive care.</p>\r\n<h2>Required Aid</h2>\r\n<p>Zarine needs 30-Lakhs in financial aid for her BMT treatment and supportive care. We kindly ask you, to donate with an open heart and generously, to support her during this phase of her life!</p>\r\n<h2>Total Fundraising Goal: INR 30,00,000</h2>','Zarine is a 10-year old girl, staying with her family in Nagpur. Her father Aslam is a farmer, her mother Ruksana is a house-wife, her elder sister is studying in 7th Std and Zarine studies in 5th Std.','Zarine','Zarine is a 10-year old girl, staying with her family in Nagpur. Her father Aslam is a farmer, her mother Ruksana is a house-wife, her elder sister is studying in 7th Std and Zarine studies in 5th Std.','','2024-08-13 09:55:09'),
	(30,'Rahil Abbas','rahil-abbas','rahil-abbas_66bae094abc84.jpg','Tuesday, 20 October, 2020','Inactive','<h2>About Rahil Abbas</h2>\r\n<p>Rahil Abbas is a 4-year old boy, who stays with his family: Father &ndash; Mr. Jahir Abbas, Mother &ndash; Mrs. Rashmi Abbas, his uncle and his grandmother. The family hails from West-Bengal, Hooghly district. They are into farming which is their main source of income. Rahil is studying in LKG at a Government school and is a very active student, he also loves playing games and spending time with the everyone at home.</p>\r\n<h2>Medical Details</h2>\r\n<p>In September 2020, Rahil&rsquo;s mother noticed that his stomach had swollen up. The concerned family took him to a government hospital in Hooghly. After a scan, the Doctor informed that his liver might have swollen up and prescribed medication for the same, however; this didn&rsquo;t help in improving in his condition. The family then took him to a government hospital in Kolkata, where he underwent a blood-test and scan. Due to the lack of facilities at the hospital, the doctor suggested that he be treated at a hospital in Bengaluru.</p>\r\n<p>In Bengaluru, the family approached HCG Hospital. At HCG, he had to undergo a corona test for which he tested negative; post which, he underwent a blood-test and PET-CT scan. He was then diagnosed with, &lsquo;Acute-Lymphoblastic-Leukemia&rsquo; (ALL). Rahil Abbas, will now have to go through: &ndash; Induction-chemotherapy, Maintenance-chemotherapy, Cranial radiation and PICC line placement. He has started with his first session of induction-chemotherapy</p>\r\n<h2>Financial Details</h2>\r\n<p>The family has spent approximately twenty-thousand (INR &ndash; 20,000/-) up till now for his treatment. The estimated cost for his treatment &ndash; INR 8,60,000/-</p>\r\n<p>Mr. Jahir being the only breadwinner of the family, is in dire need of your support in arranging the money for his son&rsquo;s treatment.</p>\r\n<p>Let&rsquo;s get together, support and contribute all we can to help Rahil and his family during this challenging time.</p>\r\n<h2>Required Aid</h2>\r\n<p>Rahil Abbas requires financial aid of, Eight Lakh Sixty Thousand Rupees (INR &ndash; 8,60,000/-) for radiation, maintenance-chemotherapy and surgery.</p>\r\n<h2>Total Fundraising Goal: INR 8,60,000</h2>','Rahil Abbas is a 4-year old boy, who stays with his family: Father â€“ Mr. Jahir Abbas, Mother â€“ Mrs. Rashmi Abbas, his uncle and his grandmother. Rahil is studying in LKG at a Government school and is a very active student.','Rahil Abbas','Rahil Abbas is a 4-year old boy, who stays with his family: Father â€“ Mr. Jahir Abbas, Mother â€“ Mrs. Rashmi Abbas, his uncle and his grandmother. Rahil is studying in LKG at a Government school and is a very active student.','','2024-08-13 09:57:00'),
	(31,'Uma Samanta','uma-samanta','uma-samanta_66bae0f0038e6.jpg','Friday, 23 October, 2020','Inactive','<h2>About Uma Samanta</h2>\r\n<p>Uma Samanta is 28-years old, from Midnapore in West-Bengal. She stays with her husband &ndash; Pallab, daughter -Khushi and her father-in-law. Her father-in-law is a farmer, husband works at an electric shop, her daughter is studying and Uma takes care of the household.</p>\r\n<h2>Medical Details</h2>\r\n<p>It all started in 2013, when Uma began experiencing back and leg pain. Her husband took her to a local hospital in Kolkata, where she got an X-ray and post-analysis; the doctor informed that there was an issue with her spinal-cord and prescribed medication. As there was no significant improvement, they went to Sri Sathya Sai Hospital in Puttaparthi, Andhra Pradesh. Here, after undergoing an MRI-Scan, the report confirmed the presence of a tumor on her spinal-cord. A surgery to remove the tumor was suggested by the doctor, who referred them to Dr.Pramod at HCG Hospital, Bengaluru; post which Uma underwent the surgery to remove the tumor.</p>\r\n<p>Six-months later when Uma was on her follow-up consultation, the doctor informed her that the tumor had recurred and suggested treatment by Injection. Uma has taken 15 injections up till now, each at the cost of INR 30,000/- and the size of the tumor has decreased. This past year has been very difficult for her and due to the pandemic she has lost out on almost a full year of treatment. The tumor increased in size and the pain intensified, she was given immediate treatment through Injection and has been informed to undergo surgery.</p>\r\n<h2>Update</h2>\r\n<p>Uma, has completed her treatment.</p>\r\n<p>Total Fundraising Goal: NA</p>','Uma Samanta is 28-years old, from Midnapore in West-Bengal. She stays with her husband â€“ Pallab, daughter -Khushi and her father-in-law. Her father-in-law is a farmer, husband works at an electric shop.','Uma Samanta','Uma Samanta is 28-years old, from Midnapore in West-Bengal. She stays with her husband â€“ Pallab, daughter -Khushi and her father-in-law. Her father-in-law is a farmer, husband works at an electric shop.','','2024-08-13 09:58:32'),
	(32,'Mohammed Saleem','mohammed-saleem','saleem-image_66bb0cb2438ae.jpg','Tuesday, 10 November, 2020','Inactive','<h2>About Mohammed Saleem</h2>\r\n<p>Mohammed Saleem is 33-years old, married to Shazia Kousar and is the father of three children; two daughters and a son. The family stays in a rented house near Guddadahalli, Bengaluru. He works as a mechanic at a garage and when at home spends most of his time with his children.</p>\r\n<h2>Medical Details</h2>\r\n<p>In 2018, Saleem would experience frequent headaches, for which the reason was unknown. After consulting a doctor and based on his suggestion, he underwent a MRI &ndash; scan at a diagnostic centre near his house. Post which the family approached a doctor with the scan reports at Apollo Hospital, wherein the doctor confirmed that Saleem was suffering from a brain-tumour. He needed to undergo a surgery in order to remove the tumour, the question was &ldquo;How would this be done?&rdquo;. A family doctor suggested that treatment could be done at HCG Hospital.</p>\r\n<p>At HCG Hospital, post the MRI &ndash; scan and going through the report; Dr.Sridhar suggested that he undergo CyberKnife Radiation Therapy. In 2019, he underwent CyberKnife and was on his follow-up consultations. After a while Saleem began experiencing severe headaches and blurred vision, this made the family consult the doctor once again. In 2020, he underwent another MRI &ndash; Scan and after getting the report had to undergo a Biopsy.</p>\r\n<p>He is yet to undergo CyberKnife Radiation Therapy. Based on the test results, he will be undergoing treatment.</p>\r\n<h2>Financial Details</h2>\r\n<p>The family has already spent 5-Lakhs until now for his treatment, by taking a loan and getting help from relatives. They have exhausted all their savings and are in need of financial support for the remaining part of his treatment.</p>\r\n<h2>Required Aid</h2>\r\n<p>Saleem requires financial aid of 8-Lakhs for CyberKnife radiation therapy and supportive care.</p>\r\n<h2>Total Fundraising Goal: INR 8,00,000</h2>','<p>Mohammed Saleem is 33-years old, married to Shazia Kousar and is the father of three children; two daughters and a son. The family stays in a rented house near Guddadahalli, Bengaluru.</p>','Mohammed Saleem','Mohammed Saleem is 33-years old, married to Shazia Kousar and is the father of three children; two daughters and a son. The family stays in a rented house near Guddadahalli, Bengaluru.','','2024-08-13 10:00:12'),
	(33,'Sonu','sonu','sonu-image_66baeb4e11bf0.jpg','Wednesday, 18 November, 2020','Inactive','<h2>About Sonu</h2>\r\n<p>Sonu is 10-years old staying with his family, his parents and a younger brother in Giridih, Jharkhand. His father Adhir Kumar is an auto-driver and earns a meagre INR 5000/- a month and his mother Gita Devi is a home maker.</p>\r\n<p>Sonu is currently studying in 1st Std in a private school near his home. He is very active and loves learning about new topics each day. After getting back home from school, Sonu enjoys watching TV and playing games with his younger brother.</p>\r\n<h2>Medical Details</h2>\r\n<p>In September 2020, Sonu&rsquo;s jaw began swelling up. Concerned about this development his parents took him to a government hospital where they informed his parents that the swelling might be due to the growth of a new tooth. A month later the size of the lump had significantly increased. Sonu&rsquo;s father then took him to consult a doctor at a private hospital, the doctor confirmed that the swelling was a tumor and it needed to be treated immediately and referred them to HCG Abdul Razzaque Ansari Cancer Hospital at Ranchi.</p>\r\n<p>At HCG Abdul Razzaque Ansari Cancer Hospital, post a check up and going through Sonu&rsquo;s recent blood reports and CT scan reports, the family was informed about the line of treatment. On 2nd November 2020, Sonu underwent a surgery to remove the tumor.</p>\r\n<p>He has completed his surgery and is recovering from his diagnosis.</p>\r\n<h2>Financial Details</h2>\r\n<p>The family has spent close to 2-lakhs until now for his surgery and treatment. They were able to do so by selling their cow, their motorbike, the family land and borrowing money from their house owner.</p>\r\n<p>All of their resources have been exhausted and they are in need of your help to arrange money for Sonu&rsquo;s supportive care and further treatment.</p>\r\n<h2>Required Aid</h2>\r\n<p>Sonu, requires financial aid of 1-lakh for his supportive care.</p>\r\n<h2>Total Fundraising Goal: INR 1,00,000</h2>','Sonu is 10-years old staying with his family, his parents and a younger brother in Giridih, Jharkhand. His father Adhir Kumar is an auto-driver and earns a meagre INR 5000/- a month and his mother Gita Devi is a home maker.','Sonu','Sonu is 10-years old staying with his family, his parents and a younger brother in Giridih, Jharkhand. His father Adhir Kumar is an auto-driver and earns a meagre INR 5000/- a month and his mother Gita Devi is a home maker.','','2024-08-13 10:42:46'),
	(34,'Tejaswini','tejaswini','tejaswini-image_66baebcd62413.jpeg','Tuesday, 5 January, 2021','Inactive','<h2>About Tejaswini</h2>\r\n<p>Tejaswini is a 13-years old and stays with her family in Davanagere. Her father Malthesh, works as a Supervisor in a Private company and her mother Neelama looks after the house. The family stay in a rented house.</p>\r\n<p>She is currently studying in 6th Std and has two siblings, a younger brother and sister. Tejaswini is not only a studious child, she is a girl with many talents. She is very interested in painting and in her free time loves to practice meditation with her family.</p>\r\n<h2>Medical Details</h2>\r\n<p>In July, she began experiencing difficulty in breathing and had developed a lump in her lymph node. Concerned, the family took her to Bapuji hospital, Davanagere. Post a blood-test, they were referred too HCG hospital, Hubli by a family member. The doctors at HCG Hubli, went through her reports and referred them to HCG hospital, Bengaluru.</p>\r\n<p>On September 31st, they consulted with Dr.Sachin at HCG Bengaluru. Here she underwent a biopsy and a few blood-tests, post which she was diagnosed with T-Acute Lymphoblastic Leukaemia. After going through her report on bone-marrow density, the family was informed that she had to undergo 4-cycles of chemotherapy and a bone-marrow transplant.</p>\r\n<p>For the next few months she will be undergoing the process of BMT.</p>\r\n<h2>Financial Details</h2>\r\n<p>The family has spent close to 12-lakhs until now by receiving help from family members and support of approximately 10-lakhs from ESI.</p>\r\n<h2>Required Aid</h2>\r\n<p>Tejaswini needs financial aid of approximately 30-Lakhs for her chemotherapy, Bone-Marrow-Transplant and Supportive Care.</p>\r\n<h2>Total Fundraising Goal: INR 30,00,000/-</h2>','Tejaswini is a 13-years old and stays with her family in Davanagere. Her father Malthesh, works as a Supervisor in a private company and her mother Neelama looks after the house. .She is currently studying in 6th Std and has two siblings, a younger brother and sister.','Tejaswini','Tejaswini is a 13-years old and stays with her family in Davanagere. Her father Malthesh, works as a Supervisor in a private company and her mother Neelama looks after the house. .She is currently studying in 6th Std and has two siblings, a younger brother and sister.','','2024-08-13 10:44:53'),
	(35,'Shravanth','shravanth','shravanth-image_66baec3894698.jpg','Friday, 22 January, 2021','Inactive','<h2>About Shravanth</h2>\r\n<p>Shravanth is 4-years old staying with his family in Dharwad. His father Mallikarjun is a farmer, his mother Nethra looks after the house and his two older sisters are studying at a government school. Due to the pandemic, Shravanth has not yet joined school.</p>\r\n<p>He is a very active child at home and spends his time playing games with his sisters and the neighbour&rsquo;s children.</p>\r\n<h2>Medical Details</h2>\r\n<p>On 14th September 2020 he had a fever and a slight swelling in his legs. This didn&rsquo;t subside, despite the fact of taken basic antibiotics. Concerned about this development, the family took him to Hubli City Hospital to get a blood-test done. The test-report revealed an increase in his WBC, which could have stemmed from Leukaemia according to the doctor. He underwent a bone-marrow test which confirmed it to be Leukaemia.</p>\r\n<p>The family was uncertain on how to proceed further, based on a suggestion from a family member they decided to come to HCG Hospital in Bengaluru to consult with Dr.Amith. After another round of bone-marrow and blood-tests, Shravanth was diagnosed with &ndash; High Risk T-cell Acute Lymphoblastic Leukaemia (T-ALL). The family was informed about the line of treatment, one-cycle of chemotherapy and a bone-marrow transplant.</p>\r\n<p>On 22nd September, Shravanth underwent his first-cycle of chemotherapy over a span of one month. However, his body didn&rsquo;t respond well to the treatment and had to undergo a bone-marrow density test. Post the results, he underwent a second-cycle of chemotherapy to reduce the count of cancer-cells. In the coming few weeks he will be undergoing a bone-marrow transplant.</p>\r\n<h2>Financial Details</h2>\r\n<p>The family has spent upto 17-lakhs for two-cycles of chemotherapy, bone-marrow test and supportive care. They were able to do so by taking a gold-loan and by borrowing money from their relatives. They have also received 3-lakhs from the CM fund and have exhausted all their financial resources.</p>\r\n<p>The family need your support in raising funds for his Bone-Marrow-Transplant, which is estimated at 22-lakhs.</p>\r\n<h2>Required Aid</h2>\r\n<p>Shravanth needs financial aid of 22-lakhs for a Bone-Marrow-Transplant and for his supportive care.</p>\r\n<h2>Total Fundraising Goal: INR 22,00,000/-</h2>','Shravanth is 4-years old staying with his family in Dharwad. His father Mallikarjun is a farmer, his mother Nethra looks after the house and his two older sisters are studying at a government school. Due to the pandemic, Shravanth has not yet joined school.','Shravanth','Shravanth is 4-years old staying with his family in Dharwad. His father Mallikarjun is a farmer, his mother Nethra looks after the house and his two older sisters are studying at a government school. Due to the pandemic, Shravanth has not yet joined school.','','2024-08-13 10:46:40'),
	(36,'Nanditha','nanditha','nanditha-image_66baec98ace25.jpg','Tuesday, 16 March, 2021','Inactive','<h2>About Nanditha</h2>\r\n<p>Nanditha is 26-years old staying with her husband Mr. Narsaiya in KG Halli, Bengaluru. Her husband works as an office boy at a textile shop and earns a mere INR10,000/- a month. Nanditha, on the other hand has completed her 2nd PUC and is a house-wife. She spends most of her time indulging in learning embroidery and making new designs on clothes.</p>\r\n<h2>Medical Details</h2>\r\n<p>It all started in 2014, she began experiencing severe pain in her right ankle, which over the next few days began swelling up. Concerned about this development, the family consulted an Orthopaedic and she underwent a round of X-Ray. Upon checking the report, the doctor informed her that she was suffering from Lymph node metastasis lung cancer; for which she underwent a tumor extraction surgery.</p>\r\n<p>On May 2020, she started facing the same issue, despite having a second successful surgery in 2015 at Hosmat hospital. The family approached HCG Hospital, where they consulted with Dr. Pramod. She went through the process of getting a MRI Scan, PET-CT Scan and X-Ray. On receiving the reports, she underwent a tumor extraction surgery on 1st Feb 2021. Post which she has been advised to take Injections; twice a day for 5-days to stop the regrowth of the tumor.</p>\r\n<h2>Update</h2>\r\n<p>She has completed her surgery and is recovering from her surgical wound. She is currently able to walk with the assistance of a walker.</p>\r\n<p>Total Fundraising Goal: NA</p>','Nanditha is 26-years old staying with her husband Mr. Narsaiya in KG Halli, Bengaluru. Her husband works as an office boy at a textile shop and earns a mere INR10,000/- a month. She spends most of her time indulging in learning embroidery and making new designs on clothes.','Nanditha','Nanditha is 26-years old staying with her husband Mr. Narsaiya in KG Halli, Bengaluru. Her husband works as an office boy at a textile shop and earns a mere INR10,000/- a month. She spends most of her time indulging in learning embroidery and making new designs on clothes.','','2024-08-13 10:48:16'),
	(37,'Abhinav','abhinav','abhinav-image_66baecf04658a.jpg','Tuesday, 16 March, 2021','Inactive','<h2>About Abhinav</h2>\r\n<p>Abhinav is 10-years old, staying with his family in Basavanagudi, Bengaluru. His father Mr. Arumugam works as a mason and his mother Mrs. Savitha is a housewife. He has an elder brother who is studying B.E 2nd year and Abhinav is studying in 4th Std.</p>\r\n<p>He is quite active when it comes to his studies and he is very energetic when it comes to playing Basketball and attends coaching classes on a regular basis to improve his skills.</p>\r\n<h2>Medical Details</h2>\r\n<p>In February 2020, Abhinav got into an altercation, which resulted in him being hit by a skate-board and he ended up with a hairline fracture in his left leg. After getting treated at a local clinic, the pain persisted over the next few weeks. Little did they know, that they were in for a shock of their lifetime.</p>\r\n<p>The family approached an Orthopaedic, where he underwent an MRI- Scan bringing to light that the pain was caused because of a different reason. They were referred to consult with Dr. Pramod at HCG Hospital, where he underwent a biopsy and PET-CT Scan; post receiving the report he was diagnosed with &lsquo;Osteosarcoma&rsquo;. Abhinav underwent surgery to remove the tumor and to control the growth of cancer cells, was suggested to 6-cycles of chemotherapy.</p>\r\n<h2>Update</h2>\r\n<p>Abhinav, has been shifted to another Hospital, where he will undergo his treatment.</p>\r\n<p>Total Fundraising Goal: NA</p>','Abhinav is 10-years old, staying with his family in Basavanagudi, Bengaluru. He is quite active when it comes to his studies and he is very energetic when it comes to playing Basketball and attends coaching classes on a regular basis to improve his skills.','Abhinav','Abhinav is 10-years old, staying with his family in Basavanagudi, Bengaluru. He is quite active when it comes to his studies and he is very energetic when it comes to playing Basketball and attends coaching classes on a regular basis to improve his skills.','','2024-08-13 10:49:44'),
	(38,'Piyush','piyush','piyush-image_66baed5c8fac7.jpeg','Tuesday, 23 March, 2021','Inactive','<h2>About Piyush</h2>\r\n<p>Piyush, is a 9-year old boy staying with his family in a rented house in Peenya, Bengaluru. His father, Mr.Suresh works in a provision store and is the sole earning member of the family; while his mother Mrs.Rekha is a house wife.</p>\r\n<p>He is studying in 4th Std and his elder brother Rohit is studying in 6th Std at Arvind International School. Piyush is very smart when it comes to his studies and is also quite talented in drawing too.</p>\r\n<h2>Medical Details</h2>\r\n<p>It all started on 24th December, 2016 when his neck started swelling up and he complained of dizziness. Concerned about this development his father took him to Manasa Hospital, Vijaynagar; where they got a blood test done. After going through the report, the doctor referred them to KIDWAI. Here, after undergoing another blood test and upon getting the results, they were informed that Piyush has T-Cell Acute Lymphoblastic Leukemia (T-ALL).</p>\r\n<p>His family then took him to HCG MSR, as he had a high-fever; he was admitted to an ICU under the supervision of Dr.Rashmi. She went through his reports and then put together his treatment plan, which was also shared with the family. Piyush underwent a total of 6-cycles of chemotherapy and completed his treatment in August 2017. He was under maintenance chemotherapy for 3-years. In August of 2020, his medication was stopped and he was on his regular follow-ups. In the month of November 2020, his right testis had swollen up &ndash; he underwent a biopsy on 12th November 2020 and it was confirmed that, there was a relapse of T-ALL. He underwent surgery on his right testis and began his chemotherapy on 1st December 2020.</p>\r\n<p>He has to undergo a total of 6-cycles of chemotherapy and radiation on his right testis.</p>\r\n<h2>Financial Details</h2>\r\n<p>The family have spent a total of 16-Lakhs until now for his treatment. They received donations from super minutes channel and support from their relatives.</p>\r\n<p>The approximate cost for his further treatment of chemotherapy is 10-Lakhs, he has to undergo radiation and BMT which will approximately cost 28-Lakhs.</p>\r\n<p>The family need your support during this time, kindly do your bit and help them raise the required funds required for treatment.</p>\r\n<h2>Required Aid</h2>\r\n<p>Piyush requires financial aid of 40-Lakhs, to undergo 4-cycles of chemotherapy, radiation and BMT treatment.</p>\r\n<h2>Total Fundraising Goal: INR 40,00,000/-</h2>','Piyush, is a 9-year old boy staying with his family in a rented house in Peenya, Bengaluru. He is studying in 4th Std at Arvind International School. Piyush is very smart when it comes to his studies and is also quite talented in drawing too.','Piyush','Piyush, is a 9-year old boy staying with his family in a rented house in Peenya, Bengaluru. He is studying in 4th Std at Arvind International School. Piyush is very smart when it comes to his studies and is also quite talented in drawing too.','','2024-08-13 10:51:32'),
	(39,'Pankaj','pankaj','pankaj-image_66baedbc89570.jpg','Friday, 26 March, 2021','Inactive','<h2>About Pankaj</h2>\r\n<p>Pankaj is a 4-year old boy, staying with his parents in a rented house in Bidar District, Gulbarga. His father Mr.Rajashekar works in a plastic sag-bag manufacturing factory and earns approximately INR 18,000/- a month, while his mother is a home maker.</p>\r\n<p>Pankaj has an elder brother Prajwal who is studying in 2nd STD, whereas Pankaj is yet to join UKG. He is a very active kid and loves spending time playing with his elder brother.</p>\r\n<h2>Medical Details</h2>\r\n<p>It started in March 2020, where he started having a few episodes of vomiting. The family took him for a consultation session with a general pediatrician in Gulbarga. After undergoing a chest-scan and blood test, he was put under medication; unfortunately this did not give him any relief.</p>\r\n<p>In April 2020, Pankaj began losing his sense of balance while walking. He underwent an MRI-Scan of his brain and a blood test, after going through the report the Doctor asked the family to consult with a neurologist, as there was a tumor present in his brain and it needed to be operated on. The family took him to Shankar hospital in Sholapur for his surgery, after the biopsy report; they confirmed that he is suffering from Posterior Fossa Meningioma &ndash; Grade II.</p>\r\n<p>The family was referred to HCG Gulbarga, where the Doctor went through the reports and Pankaj underwent a 2nd biopsy. Post getting the reports, the line of treatment as radiation was confirmed. He underwent 27-fractions and is yet to undergo 3-fractions. After completing radiation, he will be on his regular follow-up consultations.</p>\r\n<h2>Update</h2>\r\n<p>Pankaj has completed his treatment and is on his regular follow-up consultations.</p>\r\n<p>Total Fundraising Goal: NA</p>','Pankaj is a 4-year old boy, staying with his parents in a rented house in Bidar District, Gulbarga. Pankaj has an elder brother Prajwal who is studying in 2nd STD, whereas Pankaj is yet to join UKG. He is a very active kid and loves spending time playing with his elder brother.','Pankaj','Pankaj is a 4-year old boy, staying with his parents in a rented house in Bidar District, Gulbarga. Pankaj has an elder brother Prajwal who is studying in 2nd STD, whereas Pankaj is yet to join UKG. He is a very active kid and loves spending time playing with his elder brother.','','2024-08-13 10:53:08'),
	(40,'Sai Charith','sai-charith','sai-charith_66baee526bbdd.jpg','Thursday, 8 April, 2021','Inactive','<h2>About Sai Charith</h2>\r\n<p>Sai Charith is 6-years old living with his family in Hoskote,Karnataka. His father Mr.Harish is the driver of a goods-vehicle, his mother Mrs. Navyashree is a housewife and his elder sister Greeshma is studying in 2nd STD in New Horizon School, while Sai Charith is studying is in UKG. The family stay in a house that has been provided by the government.</p>\r\n<p>He is a very enthusiastic child who is good at his studies and enjoys playing games with his sister and watching movies with his family.</p>\r\n<h2>Medical Details</h2>\r\n<p>In the 1st week of January 2021, Sai Charith was down with fever. Concerned about his well-being and after consulting with the family doctor, he was put under antibiotics. However, the fever didn&rsquo;t subside, he started experiencing breathing issues for which the doctor suggested he undergo an X-Ray and a blood-test. The reports showed that water had accumulated in his lungs, the family then went to Rainbow Hospital. Here, he underwent a CT-Scan and they also collected samples of the fluid from his lungs for testing. On receiving the reports, he was diagnosed with Acute-Lymphocytic-Leukemia (ALL).</p>\r\n<p>As per the suggestion of the family doctor, they consulted Dr.Shekar Patil at HCG Hospital, Bangalore. The family was then referred to get treated under Pediatric Oncologist Dr.Intezar Mehndi, after going through his report the Doctor suggested that Sai Charith undergo 7-cycles of chemotherapy.</p>\r\n<p>Sai, started his first cycle of chemotherapy on 21st January and is currently undergoing his 5th-cycle of chemotherapy.</p>\r\n<h2>Financial Details</h2>\r\n<p>The family has already spent 10-Lakhs for his entire treatment, by taking a loan and by mortgaging their jewelry. They have received help from their relatives.</p>\r\n<p>They need your support in these challenging times.</p>\r\n<h2>Required Aid</h2>\r\n<p>Sai Charith requires financial aid of 13-Lakhs for his chemotherapy and supportive care.</p>\r\n<h2>Total Fundraising Goal: INR 13,00,000/-</h2>','Sai Charith is 6-years old living with his family in Hoskote,Karnataka. His father Mr.Harish is the driver of a goods-vehicle, his mother Mrs. Navyashree is a housewife and his elder sister Greeshma is studying in 2nd STD. He is a very enthusiastic child.','Sai Charith','Sai Charith is 6-years old living with his family in Hoskote,Karnataka. His father Mr.Harish is the driver of a goods-vehicle, his mother Mrs. Navyashree is a housewife and his elder sister Greeshma is studying in 2nd STD. He is a very enthusiastic child.','','2024-08-13 10:55:38'),
	(41,'Shridevi','shridevi','sridevi-image_66bb0c619e611.jpg','Wednesday, 28 April, 2021','Inactive','<h2>About Shridevi</h2>\r\n<p>Shridevi is a one and half year old baby girl of the two children of Mr.Dinesh Shetty and Mrs.Ranjitha Shetty. The family hails from Mangalore and they live in their own house, Mr.Dinesh is an agriculturist and is devoted to his work. The house hold chores are managed by Mrs.Ranjitha, in her free time enjoys spending time with both her children.</p>\r\n<h2>Medical Details</h2>\r\n<p>On the 25th of September 2020, Shridevi was under high fever and was taken to a general pediatrician. Although she was under medication post her visit to the Doctor, her fever didn&rsquo;t subside. A couple days later, her parents noticed a swelling in her left thigh and took her in for a consultation with a pediatrician at Manjula Nursing Home,Mangalore. Here, she underwent an X-Ray and MRI Scan; the reports revealed that her bone was infected.</p>\r\n<p>On 29th September 2020, Shridevi underwent a biopsy in Mangalore and the sample was sent for testing. Ten days later, it was confirmed that Shridevi had been suffering from Ewing Sarcoma (A cancer that most often occurs in and around the bones). She underwent 8-cycles of chemotherapy, post which the family consulted with Dr.Pramod Chinder at HCG Hospital, Bangalore; for &ndash; Tumor excision &amp; Limb Salvage surgery on 12th April 2021.</p>\r\n<p>She has completed her surgery and will be continuing her further chemotherapy sessions in Mangalore.</p>\r\n<h2>Financial Details</h2>\r\n<p>By borrowing money and mortgaging their jewels, the family has spent close to 15-Lakhs for Shridevi&rsquo;s chemotherapy and surgery. Due to the pandemic the family had to sell their Hotel, to recover losses.</p>\r\n<p>They are now in need of your support, kindly do your bit and donate as much as you can.</p>\r\n<h2>Required Aid</h2>\r\n<p>Shridevi requires financial aid of 5-Lakhs for her further treatment.</p>\r\n<h2>Total Fundraising Goal: INR 5,00,000/-</h2>','<p>Shridevi is a one and half year old baby girl of the two children of Mr.Dinesh Shetty and Mrs.Ranjitha Shetty. The family hails from Mangalore and they live in their own house, Mr.Dinesh is an agriculturist and is devoted to his work.</p>','Shridevi','Shridevi is a one and half year old baby girl of the two children of Mr.Dinesh Shetty and Mrs.Ranjitha Shetty. The family hails from Mangalore and they live in their own house, Mr.Dinesh is an agriculturist and is devoted to his work.','','2024-08-13 10:57:17'),
	(42,'Mukesh Patel','mukesh-patel','mukshesh-patel_66baef24331d6.jpeg','Tuesday, 11 May, 2021','Inactive','<h2>About Mukesh Patel</h2>\r\n<p>Mukesh Patel is a 11-year old kid of Mr. Bagaram &amp; Mrs. Meema Patel. Out of the three children Mukesh is the second child of this couple. The family hails from Rajasthan and they live in their own house of 2 rooms. However, in a small 2-Bedroom house there are a total of 14-family members staying. Which includes the patient&rsquo;s grandparents and paternal relatives.</p>\r\n<p>Mr. Bagaram is a milk supplier and is also into farming. He earns a meagre INR 10,000/- per month from this work. The entire family depend on him as the sole bread-winner.</p>\r\n<h2>Medical Details</h2>\r\n<p>Mukesh was diagnosed with Carcinoma 6-months back. Since then they have moved to a couple of hospitals for his treatment. The patient&rsquo;s parents have already paid INR 4-lakhs for his treatment until now and are currently looking for support for his surgery and chemotherapy.</p>\r\n<h2>Financial Details</h2>\r\n<p>By borrowing money and mortgaging their jewels, the family have spent close to 3.5 to 4 Lakhs for Mukesh&rsquo;s chemotherapy. Due to the pandemic his brother has also lost his job and the burden is now on Mukesh&rsquo;s father.</p>\r\n<p>They are now in dire need of your support, kindly do your bit and donate as much as you can.</p>\r\n<h2>Required Aid</h2>\r\n<p>Mukesh requires financial aid of INR 10,70,000/- for his further chemotherapy and surgery.</p>\r\n<h2>Total Fundraising Goal: INR 10,70,000/-</h2>','Mukesh Patel, is a 11 year old kid of Mr. Bagaram & Mrs. Meema Patel. Mukesh was diagnosed with carcinoma 6 months back. Since then they have moved to couple of hospitals for his treatment.','Mukesh Patel','Mukesh Patel, is a 11 year old kid of Mr. Bagaram & Mrs. Meema Patel. Mukesh was diagnosed with carcinoma 6 months back. Since then they have moved to couple of hospitals for his treatment.','','2024-08-13 10:59:08'),
	(43,'Harsha','harsha','harsha-image_66baef8dec7cd.jpg','Wednesday, 19 May, 2021','Inactive','<h2>About Harsha</h2>\r\n<p>Harsha, is a 7-year old child who is part of a joint-family staying in Ramamurthy Nagar, Bengaluru. His father Mr.Ravindra is an agriculturist and his mother Mrs.Lavanya is a house wife, the family stays in a rented house. Harsha, is the eldest child amongst his two younger sisters and a younger brother.</p>\r\n<p>He is currently studying in 1st STD at Narayana School and is very good when it comes to academics. In his free time he loves playing games with his siblings and cousins.</p>\r\n<h2>Medical Details</h2>\r\n<p>In 2020 November, Harsha developed a fever for which his family took him to a clinic. He was prescribed general antibiotics by the Doctor. However, after a couple of weeks he began throwing-up. A concerned family then took him to consult a Doctor at Shishuka Pediatric Hospital, where he underwent a CT-Scan and X-Ray. The report revealed that there was a secretion of liquid in his lungs and this needed to be removed.</p>\r\n<p>After a few days he began experiencing breathing problems and the family ended up visiting various hospitals to understand what was happening. It was at Manipal Hospital, after going through a CT &ndash;Scan that the Doctor informed them that there was the presence of Lymph Nodes, which was causing the secretion of liquid in his lungs and creating difficulty in breathing. Upon the suggestion of a relative, the family then consulted with Dr.Intezar Mehndi in January 2021. At HCG Hospital, Harsha underwent a Biopsy, CT-Scan and X-Ray post which he was diagnosed with &lsquo;Acute Lymphoblastic Leukemia&rsquo; (ALL). The family was informed about the line of treatment, being 4-cycles of chemotherapy.</p>\r\n<p>Harsha, has finished his 3rd-cycle of induction chemotherapy and further treatment is yet to be decided.</p>\r\n<h2>Financial Details</h2>\r\n<p>So far the family has spent close to 22-Lakhs, by digging into their savings, mortgaging their jewels and taking money on loan. They have exhausted all their resources and are currently requesting HCG Foundation for support.</p>\r\n<h2>Required Aid</h2>\r\n<p>Harsha, requires financial aid of approximately 15-Lakhs for his entire treatment, which includes his maintenance chemotherapy and supportive care.</p>\r\n<h2>Total Fundraising Goal: INR 15,00,000/-</h2>','Harsha, is a 7-year old child who is part of a joint-family staying in Ramamurthy Nagar, Bengaluru. Harsha, is the eldest child amongst his two younger sisters and a younger brother. In 2020 November, Harsha developed a fever for which his family took him to a clinic.','Harsha','Harsha, is a 7-year old child who is part of a joint-family staying in Ramamurthy Nagar, Bengaluru. Harsha, is the eldest child amongst his two younger sisters and a younger brother. In 2020 November, Harsha developed a fever for which his family took him to a clinic.','','2024-08-13 11:00:53'),
	(44,'Deekshitha','deekshitha','deekshitha-image_66baefe9c0cff.jpg','Monday, 14 June, 2021','Inactive','<h2>About Deekshitha</h2>\r\n<p>Deekshitha, is a 6-year old child of Mrs. Manjula and Mr. Manjunath. The family are from Bellary, Mrs. Manjula is a housewife and Mr. Manjunath works as a store assistant. Due to the pandemic all schools have been shut and Deekshitha is yet to start her 2nd Grade, at a government school in Bellary.</p>\r\n<p>Deekshitha, is very talented and loves studying and reading new books. She spends her free time in painting, practicing singing and engaging in productive games. Her dream is to become a Doctor when she grows up and help other people.</p>\r\n<h2>Medical Details</h2>\r\n<p>On the 20th of March 2021, Deekshitha fell down in her bathroom. Her concerned parents took her to a nearby Orthopedic, to undergo an X-Ray to check if she had any fractures due to the fall. The report revealed that her right-knee had severely swollen up. To get further clarity on this development, she underwent an MRI-Scan. Post-report analysis showed that she is suffering from Bone-Cancer and was referred to HCG Hospital, Bengaluru. To get a second opinion, her parents took her to KS-Hospital in Koppal, where she underwent a second round of CT-Scan and MRI-Scan; the report confirming the presence of Bone-Cancer.</p>\r\n<p>On the 26th of March 2021, Deekshitha was admitted at HCG Hospital, Bengaluru; under the consultancy of Dr. Pramod Chinder. As the previous reports weren&rsquo;t clear, she underwent a MRI-Scan, PET-CT Scan, Biopsy and Bone Marrow tests. After a detailed analysis of all the reports, she was diagnosed with &lsquo;Osteosarcoma&rsquo;. The line of treatment required is 6-cyccles of chemotherapy and surgery.</p>\r\n<p>Deekshitha, is still undergoing her 2nd-cycle of chemotherapy. Once she has completed the 3rd &ndash; cycle of chemotherapy, she will undergo surgery and then the subsequent cycles of treatment.</p>\r\n<h2>Financial Details</h2>\r\n<p>The family have spent 4.5-lakhs up till now for her treatment. The estimated cost for all the 6-cycles of chemotherapy is 16-lakhs and surgery is 12-lakhs.</p>\r\n<p>The family needs your support more than ever, during these challenging times.</p>\r\n<h2>Required Aid</h2>\r\n<p>Deekshitha, requires financial aid of 28-Lakhs for her entire treatment.</p>\r\n<h2>Total Fundraising Goal: INR 28,00,000/-</h2>','Deekshitha, is a 6-year old child of Mrs. Manjula and Mr. Manjunath. Deekshitha, is very talented and loves studying and reading new books. She spends her free time in painting, practicing singing and engaging in productive games.','Deekshitha','Deekshitha, is a 6-year old child of Mrs. Manjula and Mr. Manjunath. Deekshitha, is very talented and loves studying and reading new books. She spends her free time in painting, practicing singing and engaging in productive games.','','2024-08-13 11:02:25'),
	(45,'Kishan','kishan','kishan-image_66baf0574eef6.jpg','Tuesday, 22 June, 2021','Inactive','<h2>About Kishan</h2>\r\n<p>Kishan is 6-years old, son of Mr.Anand and Mrs.Chudamani. The family stay in a rented house at Kumaraswamy Layout, Bengaluru; paying INR 7,000/- every month. Mr. Anand works as a goods-driver and Mrs. Chudamani manages the house.</p>\r\n<p>The family have already gone through enough pain when they lost their daughter 8-years ago. Kishan is currently studying in Leo Kids School. Although, Kishan is a premature child, he is very studious and active when it comes to playing games.</p>\r\n<h2>Medical Details</h2>\r\n<p>In May 2021, Kishan was not feeling well and had developed a cough. After going for a check-up to a general physician and getting a few tests done, the Doctor mentioned that everything was normal. A week later, he was experiencing difficulty in sleeping, his concerned parents then took him to a doctor. At Medall Clumax, Bengaluru he underwent an X-Ray and the report showed that water had accumulated in his lungs. He had the water removed from his lungs and was then referred to Rainbow Hospital, Bannerghatta. Upon seeing his swollen body, he underwent a CT-Scan, Blood test and Biopsy. After going through his reports, Kishan was diagnosed with Acute-Lymphoblastic-Leukemia (ALL) and was further referred to HCG Hospital, Bengaluru.</p>\r\n<p>On 17th May 2021, the family consulted with Dr. Suma at HCG Hospital. Here he underwent a MRI-Scan, CT-Scan and Blood test. Post his tests, he had been suggested to undergo 7-cycles of chemotherapy. So far, he has completed 2-cycles of chemotherapy and is on supportive care.</p>\r\n<p>He is yet to undergo a remaining 5-cycles of treatment.</p>\r\n<h2>Financial Details</h2>\r\n<p>The estimated cost for chemotherapy and supportive is approximately 15-lakhs. By mortgaging their land, jewelry and borrowing money, the family have already spent 4.5-lakhs until now for Kishan&rsquo;s treatment.</p>\r\n<p>They have run out of financial resources and need your support.</p>\r\n<h2>Required Aid</h2>\r\n<p>Kishan, requires financial aid of 12-lakhs for his treatment. This price may vary depending on the condition of his health.</p>\r\n<h2>Total Fundraising Goal: INR 12,00,000/-</h2>','Kishan is 6-years old, son of Mr. Anand and Mrs. Chudamani. The family have already gone through enough pain when they lost their daughter 8-years ago. Kishan is currently studying in Leo Kids School. He is very studious and active when it comes to playing games.','Kishan','Kishan is 6-years old, son of Mr. Anand and Mrs. Chudamani. The family have already gone through enough pain when they lost their daughter 8-years ago. Kishan is currently studying in Leo Kids School. He is very studious and active when it comes to playing games.','','2024-08-13 11:04:15'),
	(46,'Ejas','ejas','ejas-image_66baf10361699.jpg','Monday, 23 August, 2021','Inactive','<h2>About Ejas</h2>\r\n<p>Ejas, is a 9-year old boy staying with his family, which hails from Raichur District, Karnataka. The family of 6 stay in their own &lsquo;Janata house&rsquo;, provided by the government. Ejas, is a 3rd STD student at the Milton Public School. His father, Mr. Yusif is a tailor and his mother Mrs. Shabana is a house wife. He is the third child amongst his two elder brothers and one younger sister. Ejas, is a very energetic child and loves spending his time playing with his siblings.</p>\r\n<h2>Medical Details</h2>\r\n<p>Three months ago, Ejas&rsquo;s family noticed that there was persistant lump that was growing on the left side of his neck. Concerned about this development, they took him to a hospital in Raichur, where he underwent a blood-test and a scan. Post his diagnosis, the doctor referred the family to HCG Hospital, Bengaluru. Towards the end of June, the family consulted with Dr. Sachin at HCG Hospital. After going through his previous-report, he will put into chemotherapy under Dr. Mohammed Naseer. Once he has completed 6-cycles of chemotherapy, he will then undergo BMT under Dr. Sachin Jadav.</p>\r\n<p>So far, he has completed 3-cycles of chemotherapy and has a remaining 3-cycles left to go.</p>\r\n<h2>Financial Details</h2>\r\n<p>The family come from a low-income background and have ended up spending approximately 12-lakhs until now for Ejas&rsquo;s treatment. They have exhausted their life-savings and need your support in raising funds for the remainder of his treatment.</p>\r\n<h2>Required Aid</h2>\r\n<p>Ejas, requires financial aid of 30-lakhs for his next 3-cycles of chemotherapy, BMT and supportive care.</p>\r\n<h2>Total Fundraising Goal: INR 30,00,000/-</h2>','Ejas, is a 9-year old boy staying with his family, which hails from Raichur District, Karnataka. The family of 6 stay in their own â€˜Janata houseâ€™, provided by the government. Ejas, is a 3rd STD student at the Milton Public School.','Ejas','Ejas, is a 9-year old boy staying with his family, which hails from Raichur District, Karnataka. The family of 6 stay in their own â€˜Janata houseâ€™, provided by the government. Ejas, is a 3rd STD student at the Milton Public School.','','2024-08-13 11:07:07'),
	(47,'Akash Yadav','akash-yadav','akash-yadav_66bafc8879f18.jpg','Monday, 23 August, 2021','Inactive','<h2>About Akash Yadav</h2>\r\n<p>Akash Yadav, is the 1-year toddler of Mr.Ravirajan and Mrs.Sunitha, he is the youngest child amongst 3-elder sisters. The family hail from Chhatarpur, Jharkhand and stay in their own house. Mr.Ravirajan, is an agriculturist and Mrs.Sunitha, is a home-maker. Akash, is a very playful young child and the family shower him with love and affection. His sisters enjoy spending time with him very much.</p>\r\n<h2>Medical Details</h2>\r\n<p>In June 2021, Akash started having several episodes of vomiting and his stomach had swollen up. His parents took him to a private hospital in Jaldege, Jharkhand, where he underwent a blood-test and X-ray. Post-report analysis revealed that he was suffering from &lsquo;Wilms Tumor&rsquo;. Akash, was put under observation and was prepared to undergo a tumor removal surgery. Once the surgery was completed, the family were asked to approach HCG Hospital, Ranchi.</p>\r\n<p>At HCG Hospital, the family consulted with Dr. Aftab Alam Ansari, who after observing Akash&rsquo;s condition and studying his reports suggested that he undergo radiation and continue with chemotherapy.</p>\r\n<p>Akash, is undergoing radiation and the number of chemotherapy cycles will be decided upon, post receiving his radiation report.</p>\r\n<h2>Financial Details</h2>\r\n<p>The family come from a very low-income background and finding steady work is a challenge. They have spent up-to 3-lakhs, by mortgaging their land and by borrowing money. They need your help during these troubled times.</p>\r\n<h2>Required Aid</h2>\r\n<p>Akash Yadav, requires financial support of approximately 3-lakhs for his further chemotherapy and supportive care.</p>\r\n<h2>Total Fundraising Goal: INR 3,00,000/-</h2>','Akash Yadav, is the 1-year toddler of Mr. Ravirajan and Mrs. Sunitha, he is the youngest child amongst 3-elder sisters. In June 2021, Akash started having several episodes of vomiting and his stomach had swollen up.','Akash Yadav','Akash Yadav, is the 1-year toddler of Mr. Ravirajan and Mrs. Sunitha, he is the youngest child amongst 3-elder sisters. In June 2021, Akash started having several episodes of vomiting and his stomach had swollen up.','','2024-08-13 11:56:16'),
	(48,'Byresh','byresh','byresh-image_66bb077340571.jpg','Monday, 23 August, 2021','Inactive','<h2>About Byresh</h2>\r\n<p>Byresh is a 3-year old child, the only son of Mr. Hemanth Kumar and Mrs. Sowmya. The family stay in their own house at Ramanagara. Here, Mr. Hemanth runs a provision store and Mrs. Sowmya is a teacher at a Private School. Byresh, was going to Anganwadi to study, however due to the lockdown he has had to stay home. Being the only child to his parents, his parents take great care of him and love him very much.</p>\r\n<h2>Medical Details</h2>\r\n<p>From the time Byresh was 2-month old baby, he was suffering from a deficiency of blood-cells. The family consulted a doctor at Rajarajeshwari Hospital. Here, after getting a few blood tests done, he was diagnosed with Beta-Thalassemia-Major. The line of treatment suggested was either &ndash; a blood-transfusion or a BMT.</p>\r\n<p>The family then decided to approach HCG Hospital and consulted with Dr. Rashmi. After observing his condition, studying his reports and taking into consideration his age &ndash; a blood transfusion was suggested, which he has undergone. As of July 2021, he has started with his BMT treatment and further line of treatment will be decided based on his response to BMT.</p>\r\n<h2>Current Update</h2>\r\n<p>It is with a heavy heart that we share this update with you. Our cancer-fighter Byresh is no longer with us. We convey our deepest condolences to the family. May his soul rest-in-peace.</p>','Byresh is a 3-year old child, the only son of Mr. Hemanth Kumar and Mrs. Sowmya. The family stay in their own house at Ramanagara. Here, Mr. Hemanth runs a provision store and Mrs. Sowmya is a teacher at a Private School. His parents take great care of him and love him very much.','Byresh','Byresh is a 3-year old child, the only son of Mr. Hemanth Kumar and Mrs. Sowmya. The family stay in their own house at Ramanagara. Here, Mr. Hemanth runs a provision store and Mrs. Sowmya is a teacher at a Private School. His parents take great care of him and love him very much.','','2024-08-13 12:42:51'),
	(49,'Raja','raja','raja-image_66bb07f2280c6.jpg','Wednesday, 29 September, 2021','Inactive','<h2>About Raja</h2>\r\n<p>Raja is the 9-year old son of Mr. Ahmed Ali and Mrs. Najeema, he has a younger brother named Rasool, who is 3-years old. The family hail from West-Bengal and stay in their own house. Mr. Ahmed is a daily wage worker and Mrs. Najeema is a house wife. Raja, is studies in 4th STD at a Government school in Murshidabad, West Bengal.</p>\r\n<h2>Medical Details</h2>\r\n<p>Six months prior, Raja was experiencing severe pain in his chest; concerned about this development his family took him to a Government Hospital in Murshidabad. Here, he got a blood test and X-ray done, post going through his report the Doctor informed that, there was liquid secretion in his left lung which needed to be removed. He underwent a minor surgery to extract the water from his left lung, however, there was a concern regarding the color (Red) of the fluid that was removed. Upon inspection, the Doctor then suspected that he might have a tumor in his lung.</p>\r\n<p>The family were the referred to a Government Hospital in Kolkata, here he underwent certain Blood tests, X-ray, a CT-scan and a PET-CT-scan. After receiving the results, it was confirmed that Raja was suffering from Lung cancer. They were further referred to visit a Hospital in Bengaluru.</p>\r\n<p>In the month of August, they first visited Ambedkar Hospital, Bengaluru; where he underwent a biopsy. They were then referred to HCG Hospital, Malleshwaram; where he began his chemotherapy treatment. Raja has currently finished 4-cycles of chemotherapy and has a pending 10-cycles of chemotherapy left. If required a post-treatment surgery will also be needed.</p>\r\n<h2>Financial Details</h2>\r\n<p>By borrowing money from their family members, they have spent 3-Lakhs until now for his treatment. The family are currently being supported by HCG Foundation, as they have exhausted all their financial resources.</p>\r\n<h2>Required Aid</h2>\r\n<p>Raja requires financial aid of approximately 5-Lakhs for the remaining 10-cycles of chemotherapy.</p>\r\n<h2>Total Fundraising Goal: INR 5,00,000/-</h2>','Raja is the 9-year old son of Mr. Ahmed Ali and Mrs. Najeema, he has a younger brother named Rasool, who is 3-years old. Raja, is studies in 4th STD at a Government school in Murshidabad, West Bengal. He was experiencing severe pain in his chest.','Raja','Raja is the 9-year old son of Mr. Ahmed Ali and Mrs. Najeema, he has a younger brother named Rasool, who is 3-years old. Raja, is studies in 4th STD at a Government school in Murshidabad, West Bengal. He was experiencing severe pain in his chest.','','2024-08-13 12:44:58'),
	(50,'Pavitra','pavitra','pavitra-image_66bb0844130ea.jpg','Tuesday, 22 February, 2022','NA','<h2>About Pavitra</h2>\r\n<p>Pavitra, is the 5-year old daughter; the 3rd child out of the four children of Mr. Yankappa and Mrs. Devamma. The family hail from Yadgir, Karnataka. Mr.Yankappa, is a daily wage worker and earns about INR 8000/- per month. His wife, Mrs.Devamma is a homemaker. The family were planning on admitting their second child to school this year, they were shocked to learn that their daughter is diagnosed with, &lsquo;Cellular Tumor&rsquo; and that she needed to undergo surgery.</p>\r\n<p>As a parent it is not easy seeing their beloved child suffer at such a young age. The family have dedicated their entire time and effort focusing on one goal! &lsquo;To see their beloved child laughing and active as she was&rsquo;.</p>\r\n<h2>Medical Details</h2>\r\n<p>Pavitra, had developed a persistent fever coupled with a severe headache. The family consulted a clinician nearby their home, where she underwent a few tests and was diagnosed with, &lsquo;Cellular Tumor&rsquo;. The doctor referred them to NIMHANS-Bengaluru, as they couldn&rsquo;t treat her case; and considering her critical state, she was immediately shifted to HCG Hospital, for surgery. On 29th December 2021, she underwent surgery under Dr.Gaurav Shankar Madikari and has since been coming for her follow up treatment.</p>\r\n<h2>Current Update</h2>\r\n<p>Pavitra has completed her surgery and is currently on her follow-up treatment.</p>','','Pavitra','Pavitra, is the 5-year old daughter; the 3rd child out of the four children of Mr. Yankappa and Mrs. Devamma. She is dearly loved at home and is very enthusiastic and playful. The family hail from Yadgir, Karnataka.','','2024-08-13 12:46:20'),
	(51,'Tejashree K','tejashree-k','tejashree-k-image_66bb08b1c2588.jpg','Tuesday, 22 February, 2022','Inactive','<h2>About Tejashree</h2>\r\n<p>Having lost her father and her brother, 13-year old Tejashree is the only daughter to her mother; who works as a house-maid. She is currently in 8th Grade, and is a studious young girl and also very active in participating in sports at her school. She is a girl who loves spending her time in the comfort of nature.</p>\r\n<p>She has currently been diagnosed with, &lsquo;Right Adrenal Mass&rsquo; and needs to undergo surgery immediately. Her Mother, has been praying day-in and day-out, for her daughter so that she gets better.</p>\r\n<h2>Medical Details</h2>\r\n<p>The issue began when Tejashree began experiencing pain in her abdomen. Upon consulting a Doctor at a local hospital in Tumkur, they were asked to meet Dr.Abhilash Narayana at HCG Hospital, Bengaluru.</p>\r\n<p>At HCG Hospital, she was suggested to undergo surgery at the earliest, following which she is to come in for her regular follow-up tests and scans.</p>\r\n<p>She has completed her surgery and is yet to start her follow-up consultations, scans, tests and treatment.</p>\r\n<h2>Financial Details</h2>\r\n<p>By exhausting her financial savings and mortgaging her jewels, her Mother has managed to cover the cost for her surgery.</p>\r\n<p>Let&rsquo;s come together and help the family in their time of need!</p>\r\n<h2>Required Aid</h2>\r\n<p>Tejashree, requires financial aid of INR 2,04,450/- for further tests, scans, follow-up consultations and treatment.</p>\r\n<p>They have applied for the CM &amp; PM Fund and are also being supporetd by HCG Foundation.</p>\r\n<h2>Total Fundraising Goal: INR 2,04,450/-</h2>','Tejashree, is a 13-year old only daughter of her mother. She is currently in 8th Grade, and is a studious young girl and also very active in participating in sports at her school. She is a girl who loves spending her time in the comfort of nature.','Tejashree K','Tejashree, is a 13-year old only daughter of her mother. She is currently in 8th Grade, and is a studious young girl and also very active in participating in sports at her school. She is a girl who loves spending her time in the comfort of nature.','','2024-08-13 12:48:09'),
	(52,'Naveen R','naveen-r','naveen-r-image_66bb0914c0dc7.jpg','Friday, 18 March, 2022','Inactive','<h2>About Naveen</h2>\r\n<p>Naveen is 42-years old, he is the sole bread-winner for his family. He currently takes care of his parents, his Father is aged 90-years and his Mother is 82-years old. He has a sister who is married. Naveen, was working with a transport agency associated with Jet-Airways, he has currently stopped working as he has been diagnosed with, &lsquo;Carcinoma Colon Cancer&rsquo;.</p>\r\n<p>The family is currently surviving on the minimal pension fund that have accumulated and are currently seeking all the monetary support they can get.</p>\r\n<h2>Medical Details</h2>\r\n<p>In June 2021, Naveen was admitted at HCG Hospital, Bengaluru. At HCG he was treated by Dr.Srinivas B. J, so far Naveen has undergone surgery and 6-cycles of chemotherapy. The total cost for the same surmounting to INR 4,50,000 /- the family have managed to pay the cost until now and have exhausted all their resources.</p>\r\n<p>The further plan of treatment involves FAPI Therapy, for which the family needs INR 2,25,000 /- As the drug used for the treatment needs to be brought in from Germany.</p>\r\n<h2>Financial Details</h2>\r\n<p>The family have spent all their life savings for the initial stages of treatment, to see their son back on his feet. The family have approached HCG Foundation, to help them raise INR 2,25,000/-</p>\r\n<h2>Required Aid</h2>\r\n<p>Naveen needs your help during these challenging times, as he needs to undergo FAPI Therapy which will cost INR 2,25,000/- .</p>\r\n<p>Please, let&rsquo;s come together and help raise the funds for Naveen.</p>\r\n<h2>Total Fundraising Goal: INR 2,25,000/-</h2>','Naveen, is 42-years old, currently working for a transport agency associated with Jet-Airways. He is the sole bread winner of the family. He has been diagnosed with, â€˜Carcinoma Colon Cancerâ€™. The family have been surviving on the minimal family pension so far.','Naveen R','Naveen, is 42-years old, currently working for a transport agency associated with Jet-Airways. He is the sole bread winner of the family. He has been diagnosed with, â€˜Carcinoma Colon Cancerâ€™. The family have been surviving on the minimal family pension so far.','','2024-08-13 12:49:48'),
	(53,'Sidvin B','sidvin-b','sidvin-b-image_66bb0980473ed.jpg','Wednesday, 13 April, 2022','Inactive','<h2>About Sidvin</h2>\r\n<p>Sidvin is an athletic, smart, studious and talented young adult who is pursuing his 1st year Engineering. He is the eldest child in his family and has a younger sister. The unfortunate demise of his father Vidhyadhar last month; has left the family in a state shock. Mr.Vidhyadhar, was a farmer and the sole-breadwinner for the family.</p>\r\n<p>Amidst all the grief and loss, Sidvin is managing to stay present and is focusing on his studies. Sidvin&rsquo;s mother has been hoping and praying that her Son recovers completely. The loss of her Husband, has weighed down heavily on her and she cannot lose her son too. Her children are all that she has left.</p>\r\n<h2>Medical Details</h2>\r\n<p>Sidvin had developed a fever which hadn&rsquo;t subsided for a while, his body temperature wasn&rsquo;t reducing either. Concerned about this, his family immediately consulted a Doctor at a clinic nearby their home. They were further referred to HCG Hospital, Bengaluru. At HCG, the consulted with Dr.Intezar Mehdi, who, after conducting a few tests, diagnosed Sidvin with Osteosarcoma. This is a type of bone cancer that impacts the cells that form and maintain bones.</p>\r\n<p>His family were able to bear the cost of his initial surgery and 3-cycles of chemotherapy, by utilizing their savings, borrowing money and from the support of the CM fund. It has become quite clear, post the demise of his father who was the sole-breadwinner for the family, they are having a challenging time to manage their day to day expenses &ndash; let alone covering the cost for the remaining 3-cycles of chemotherapy.</p>\r\n<h2>Financial Details</h2>\r\n<p>Sidvin, is yet to undergo his remaining 3-cycles of chemotherapy which will cost his family an approximate of INR 5, 00,000/-. They have exhausted all their savings and mortgaged their jewellery so far. The family have run out of financial options.</p>\r\n<p>His mother has been doing everything in her capacity to raise the money needed, so that her son may undergo treatment and get better. She has being praying day in and day for her son and for funds to be raised. We at HCG Foundation, request you all to come together and help raise the required amount for Sidvin and help make a difference in his life.</p>\r\n<h2>Required Aid</h2>\r\n<p>Sidvin, requires financial aid of INR 5,00,000/- for the remaining 3-cycles of chemotherapy.</p>\r\n<h2>Total Fundraising Goal: INR 5,00,000/-</h2>','Sidvin is an athletic, smart, studious and talented young adult who is pursuing his 1st year Engineering. The unfortunate demise of his father Vidhyadhar last month; has left the family in a state shock. Mr.Vidhyadhar, was a farmer and the sole-breadwinner for the family.','Sidvin B','Sidvin is an athletic, smart, studious and talented young adult who is pursuing his 1st year Engineering. The unfortunate demise of his father Vidhyadhar last month; has left the family in a state shock. Mr.Vidhyadhar, was a farmer and the sole-breadwinner for the family.','','2024-08-13 12:51:36'),
	(54,'Avinash','avinash','avinash-image_66bb09ee069ff.jpg','Tuesday, 26 April, 2022','Inactive','<h2>About Avinash</h2>\r\n<p>Avinash, is an 11-year old child diagnosed with Pediatric Myelodysplastic Syndrome (MDS) &ndash; a form of cancer manifested by an impediment in blood cell production. Avinash comes from Gulbarga, staying with his parents and brothers. Three years ago the family lost their eldest son who was also diagnosed with Pediatric MDS, they still mourn the loss of their beloved child each day.</p>\r\n<p>Avinash&rsquo;s older, 8th-standard brother Mukesh is Avinash&rsquo;s only company at home succeeding the tragic demise of the family&rsquo;s eldest son. Despite these insufferable circumstances, Avinash kindles the youthful effervescence within him by engaging in activities he enjoys such as playing football and consuming telecast media; most inspiring of all, Avinash values his academic life and is keen on returning to school after his treatment period elapses. Avinash&rsquo;s parents devote every iota of strength they&rsquo;re capable of mustering in pursuit of the wellbeing of their children.</p>\r\n<p>The unfavorable financial scenario they find themselves in does little to inhibit the fervor with which they have committed themselves to ensure Avinash&rsquo;s fate is different from that of their beloved eldest son&rsquo;s; however, the economic deprivation that the family is subjected to renders them incapable of availing high quality medical intervention.</p>\r\n<h2>Medical Details</h2>\r\n<p>Succeeding a concerningly low blood count reading, Avinash was taken to a local hospital in Gulbarga where a series of tests revealed to the Doctor the pediatric MDS that he had developed. Avinash was then referred to Dr.Sachin at HCG Hospital, Bengaluru where he was admitted in January of 2022. Avinash, is currently planned to undergo a Bone Marrow Transplant (BMT).</p>\r\n<h2>Financial Details</h2>\r\n<p>The overall cost of Avinash&rsquo;s treatment is estimated to be INR 25,00,000/-. The family have received financial aid for the treatment from governmental relief funds (CM and PM funds) and from crowd-funding organization Ketto.</p>\r\n<p>The severity of their financial inadequacy and the exhaustion of their hand-sourced funds for the initial treatment has led them to further seek support from the HCG Foundation. Avinash&rsquo;s parents can do no more than assure themselves of their son&rsquo;s wellbeing on the basis of a sliver of hope &ndash; one which is thinning by the day.</p>\r\n<h2>Required Aid</h2>\r\n<p>Subsequent to the BMT , further consultation and Avinash&rsquo;s follow-up treatment will require an additional INR 10,00,000/- .</p>\r\n<h2>Total Fundraising Goal: INR 10,00,000/-</h2>','Avinash, is an 11-year old child diagnosed with Pediatric Myelodysplastic Syndrome (MDS) â€“ a form of cancer manifested by an impediment in blood cell production. Three years ago the family lost their eldest son who was also diagnosed with Pediatric MDS, they still mourn the loss of their beloved child each day.','Avinash','Avinash, is an 11-year old child diagnosed with Pediatric Myelodysplastic Syndrome (MDS) â€“ a form of cancer manifested by an impediment in blood cell production. Three years ago the family lost their eldest son who was also diagnosed with Pediatric MDS, they still mourn the loss of their beloved child each day.','','2024-08-13 12:53:26'),
	(55,'Manasvi S','manasvi-s','manasvi-s-image_66bb0a4e3a269.jpg','Monday, 9 May, 2022','Inactive','<h2>About Manasvi</h2>\r\n<p>Manasvi is 5-years old and the only child to her parents, Mr.Siddalinga and Mrs. Vasundara. The family reside in a rented house in Bengaluru. An active and bubbly child, this family of three is only filled with joy, laughter and love. Manasvi, has been diagnosed with B-Cell ALL (Acute-Lymphoblastic-Leukemia), which is a form of cancer that affects the B-Cells in the immune system, the disease starts in the bone-marrow.</p>\r\n<p>As she is the only child, her parents are currently under a lot of mental and emotional stress that one cannot even begin to imagine. Despite their pain and trauma, they are doing all they can to make sure their daughter recovers soon.</p>\r\n<h2>Medical Details</h2>\r\n<p>In the month of September 2021, Manasvi had developed a high fever and was continuously vomiting on a regular basis. Concerned about this development, the family brought her in for consultation to Dr.Prakash, General Pediatrics. She underwent a blood-test and was then diagnosed with &lsquo;B-Cell ALL&rsquo;, (Acute-Lymphoblastic-Leukemia).</p>\r\n<p>Manasvi, was then referred to Dr. Rasmi P at HCG MSR on 19th September 2021. She was advised to undergo BFM-2002 based chemotherapy for initial treatment.</p>\r\n<h2>Financial Details</h2>\r\n<p>So far the family have spent INR 12,00,000/- for BFM-2002 chemotherapy and supportive care. They have exhausted all their financial resources and currently need help to raise funds for the remaining part of their daughter&rsquo;s treatment. They are also receiving support from HCG Foundation.</p>\r\n<p>Please, let&rsquo;s get together in these challenging times for the family and help them raise the money they need, so that they can save their daughter.</p>\r\n<h2>Required Aid</h2>\r\n<p>Manasvi, requires financial aid of INR 10,00,000/- for her follow-up treatment and consultations.</p>\r\n<h2>Total Fundraising Goal: INR 10,00,000/-</h2>','Manasvi is 5-years old and the only child to her parents, Mr. Siddalinga and Mrs. Vasundara. The family reside in a rented house in Bengaluru. As she is the only child, her parents are currently under a lot of mental and emotional stress that one cannot even begin to imagine.','Manasvi S','Manasvi is 5-years old and the only child to her parents, Mr. Siddalinga and Mrs. Vasundara. The family reside in a rented house in Bengaluru. As she is the only child, her parents are currently under a lot of mental and emotional stress that one cannot even begin to imagine.','','2024-08-13 12:55:02'),
	(56,'Jaden','jaden','jaden-image_66bb0af3e39b7.jpg','Friday, 3 June, 2022','Inactive','<h2>About Jaden</h2>\r\n<p>Jaden, is a 3-year-old child who has been diagnosed with &ldquo;T-Cell ALL (Acute Lymphoblastic Leukemia). He comes from lower-middle class family, his Father is a gym instructor and Mother works at a private sector company. The family stay in a rented house in Bengaluru.</p>\r\n<p>Jaden is an enthusiastic child and the only child to his parents. His parents love for him is boundless. So, one can imagine how devastated they would have been when they learnt of his diagnosis of T-Cell ALL They have been working extremely hard to arrange money for his treatment. This time has been extremely challenging for the family emotionally and mentally.</p>\r\n<h2>Medical Details</h2>\r\n<p>Jaden was taken to their family doctor with nasal issues, persistent fever and repeated URTI &ndash; Symptoms, after consultation, he was suspected to have &lsquo;Acute Leukemia&rsquo; and was rushed to HCG Hospital, Bengaluru.</p>\r\n<p>After thorough evaluations at the pediatrics department, he has been diagnosed with &lsquo;T-CELL ALL&rsquo; (Acute Lymphoblastic Leukemia). The initial treatment &ndash; Induction treatment as per BFM-ALL 90 protocol and the remainder of the treatment will be chemotherapy.</p>\r\n<h2>Financial Details</h2>\r\n<p>The family have spent close to &lsquo;INR 8-Lakhs&rsquo;, so far for Jaden&rsquo;s chemotherapy and supportive care (Currently On-going); under the supervision of Dr. Intezar Mehdi. They have exhausted all their savings and are also receiving financial support from HCG Foundation.</p>\r\n<h2>Required Aid</h2>\r\n<p>Jaden requires a further amount of &lsquo;INR 5-Lakhs&rsquo;, for his follow-up treatments and consultation.</p>\r\n<h2>Total Fundraising Goal: INR 5,00,000/-</h2>','Jaden, is a 3-year-old child who has been diagnosed with â€œT-Cell ALL (Acute Lymphoblastic Leukemia). Jaden is an enthusiastic child and the only child to his parents. His parents love for him is boundless.','Jaden','Jaden, is a 3-year-old child who has been diagnosed with â€œT-Cell ALL (Acute Lymphoblastic Leukemia). Jaden is an enthusiastic child and the only child to his parents. His parents love for him is boundless.','','2024-08-13 12:57:47'),
	(57,'Iqra','iqra','iqra-image_66bb0b5342708.jpg','Tuesday, 28 June, 2022','Inactive','<h2>About Iqra</h2>\r\n<p>Iqra Banu is a 11-year old girl who comes from a middle-class family in Tumkuru, Karnataka. Her father is a butcher and mother is a home-maker. Iqra is the first child to her parents and has a younger sister. She is studying in 6th Std and has currently discontinued from school due to her diagnosis. A once enthusiastic and loving child in the family, has now become very reserved, because of the pain she has been silently suffering.</p>\r\n<p>The journey over the last few months hasn&rsquo;t been easy on the parents either, as they witness their daughter close of from the world. They have been a pillar of support day-in and day-out for Iqra and are doing everything in their power to make sure she gets better.</p>\r\n<h2>Medical Details</h2>\r\n<p>Iqra had a persistent fever that despite after having antibiotics didn&rsquo;t subside. The family took her to a clinician, who further referred them to HCG Hospital, Bengaluru. At HCG, they consulted with Dr. Intezar Mehdi, who after conducting thorough evaluations diagnosed her with &lsquo;T-CELL (ALL), Acute-Lymphoblastic-Leukemia&rsquo; (Blood Cancer).</p>\r\n<p>After educating the family about her condition and explaining the procedures involved for treatment, Iqra was placed under the care and supervision Dr.Intezar and his team. She was put under supportive care and the initial treatment being Induction Chemotherapy.</p>\r\n<h2>Financial Details</h2>\r\n<p>The family have spent close to INR 9,80,080 /- for her treatment so far, which includes the chemotherapy and supportive care. They have exhausted all their resources and are currently being supported by HCG Foundation.</p>\r\n<p>If we can all join hands and help support Iqra and her family, it would mean the world to them. Help us raise the funds needed for her remaining treatment.</p>\r\n<h2>Required Aid</h2>\r\n<p>Iqra requires financial aid of INR 5-Lakhs for her follow-up treatment and consultation.</p>\r\n<h2>Total Fundraising Goal: INR 5,00,000/-</h2>','Iqra Banu is a 11-year old girl who comes from a middle-class family in Tumkuru, Karnataka. The journey over the last few months hasnâ€™t been easy on the parents either, as they witness their daughter close-off from the world.','Iqra','Iqra Banu is a 11-year old girl who comes from a middle-class family in Tumkuru, Karnataka. The journey over the last few months hasnâ€™t been easy on the parents either, as they witness their daughter close-off from the world.','','2024-08-13 12:59:23'),
	(58,'Abhishek','abhishek','abhishek-image_66bb0bbedb962.jpg','Monday, 23 January, 2023','Inactive','<h2>About Abhishek</h2>\r\n<p>Abhishek is a lively, sporty and active 19 year old living in a village near Dandeli, North Karnataka, with an extremely loving and supportive family. As a single child, he is exceptionally adored by his mother and father. Much like all energetic young teens, he thrives on playing sports like football and kabbadi. When he is not exerting too much physical energy, he enjoys being in the company of close friends, sharing a few laughs with an infectious demeanor. In addition, Abhishek is academically inclined and devotes concentrated time to his studies. He is studying PUC at ITI and is keen on resuming his studies. He comes from an impoverished background, consequently making it strenuous for his parents to finance his medical treatment. His father is a farmer who works as a laborer and his mother is a house wife. As an only child Abhishek bears the responsibility of taking care of his family in the future.</p>\r\n<p>The journey over the last few months hasn&rsquo;t been easy on the parents either, as they witness their daughter close of from the world. They have been a pillar of support day-in and day-out for Iqra and are doing everything in their power to make sure she gets better.</p>\r\n<h2>Medical Details</h2>\r\n<p>About 3 months ago, Abhishek complained of intense pain in his legs. He found it tremendously burdensome to walk. Gravely concerned, his parents transported him to a general physician who practiced medicine in the same village. After a series of grueling tests, the family received the devastating news that Abhishek is suffering from right leg spinal tumor, a complicated form of bone cancer. Despite being burdened by the weight of this traumatic news, his parents took immediate action and admitted him into a government hospital situated in Dandeli.</p>\r\n<p>With a dejected heart, Abhishek embarked on the first step of a journey of painful treatment. Unfortunately, his health condition showed no improvement with the current treatment leaving his family and him in low in spirits. Following the unsuccessful treatment, his physician referred him to Dr. Pramod Chinder at HCG KR Hospital where he was admitted in September 2022. Upon observing Abhishek&rsquo;s condition, Dr. Pramod performed immediate Limb Salvage Surgery</p>\r\n<h2>Financial Details</h2>\r\n<p>The cost of Limb Salvage Surgery is INR 6 lacs. Determined to restore Abhishek&rsquo;s poor health, his parents promptly sold the land they owned to pay for the surgery. Helpless, without any financial resources and the sheer extremity of the cost of chemotherapy has led Abhishek&rsquo;s parents to seek further financial assistance.</p>\r\n<h2>Required Aid</h2>\r\n<p>Abhishek&rsquo;s chemotherapy and follow-up treatment will cost a further INR 5,00,000</p>\r\n<h2>Total Fundraising Goal: INR 5,00,000/-</h2>','Abhishek is a lively, sporty and active 19 year old living in a village near Dandeli, North Karnataka, with an extremely loving and supportive family. As a single child, he is exceptionally adored by his mother and father. Much like all energetic young teens, he thrives on playing sports like football and kabbadi.','Abhishek','Abhishek is a lively, sporty and active 19 year old living in a village near Dandeli, North Karnataka, with an extremely loving and supportive family. As a single child, he is exceptionally adored by his mother and father. Much like all energetic young teens, he thrives on playing sports like football and kabbadi.','','2024-08-13 13:01:10'),
	(59,'Sangamesh','sangamesh','sangamesh-image_66bb0c32b9aab.jpg','Tuesday, 3 January, 2023','Inactive','<h2>About Sangamesh</h2>\r\n<p>Sangamesh Simpi, a SSLC student, is an ambitious and talented 15 year old boy residing in a remote village in Bijapur. Sangamesh is an exceptional student. Despite his illness, which rendered him unable to walk to school, Sangamesh remains determined to overcome the odds to resume and flourish in his studies. Sangamesh aspires to be a successful engineer and is working hard to achieve his dreams and goals. One can see the immense potential he possesses. He is a boy of many talents and interests. Sangamesh is a learner. He spends dedicated time studying and reading books and newspapers. When he is not poring over books, he takes delight in playing football and cricket at school.</p>\r\n<p>Sangamesh comes from a caring family. His father, an electrician, is the sole earning member in the family. His mother is a house-wife and his younger brother is in the 6th standard. His parents praise his responsible nature and consider him the glue that keeps the family together. Armed with a thoughtful nature, Sangamesh has pledged to pay his way through higher education to reduce the financial burden on his parents.</p>\r\n<h2>Medical Details</h2>\r\n<p>In early September 2022, Sangamesh complained of a sharp pain and noticed swelling in his left knee. Troubled by the pain, his parents took him to a nearby physician for a check-up. Unable to determine the root cause of the pain and swelling, the physician promptly referred Sangamesh to a more capable doctor in the district. What came next was completely unexpected. The FNAC cancer test conducted at Dr. Karigoudar Diagnostic Laboratory revealed that Sangamesh is suffering from Osteogenic Sarcoma of the upper left Tibia, a deadly form of musculoskeletal cancer. To say the least, Sangamesh and his family were heart-broken and left with many tears to bear. With depleting psychological strength and hope his family had left, they transported Sangamesh to HCG Hospital Bangalore to Consult Dr. Shekar Patil. This began his arduous journey of medical treatment.</p>\r\n<h2>Financial Details</h2>\r\n<p>The estimated cost of three cycles of chemotherapy and surgery is INR 9,45,000. With great difficulty, his family has managed to raise INR 1,00,000 to pay for his treatment. Due to their insufficient financial resources, they are all out of options. The family has turned to the HCG Foundation for assistance.</p>\r\n<h2>Required Aid</h2>\r\n<p>Sangamesh requires a further INR 8,45,000/- for his entire treatment, which includes chemotherapy and surgery.</p>\r\n<h2>Total Fundraising Goal: INR 8,45,000/-</h2>','Sangamesh Simpi, a SSLC student, is an ambitious and talented 15 year old boy residing in a remote village in Bijapur. Sangamesh is an exceptional student. Despite his illness, which rendered him unable to walk to school, Sangamesh remains determined to overcome the odds to resume and flourish in his studies.','Sangamesh','Sangamesh Simpi, a SSLC student, is an ambitious and talented 15 year old boy residing in a remote village in Bijapur. Sangamesh is an exceptional student. Despite his illness, which rendered him unable to walk to school, Sangamesh remains determined to overcome the odds to resume and flourish in his studies.','','2024-08-13 13:03:06');

